Ä&␀␀␀␀ˇˇ␀Çol>␀␀,7:headers;1681:40:4:Date,29:Mon, 06 Apr 2026 11:32:38 GMT,]52:12:Content-Type,32:text/event-stream; charset=utf-8,]31:17:Transfer-Encoding,7:chunked,]28:10:Connection,10:keep-alive,]28:13:Cache-Control,8:no-cache,]52:38:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-limit,7:2000000,]56:42:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-remaining,7:1970000,]66:38:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T11:32:37Z,]52:39:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-limit,6:400000,]56:43:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-remaining,6:400000,]67:39:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T11:32:36Z,]45:34:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-limit,4:4000,]49:38:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-remaining,4:3999,]62:34:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-reset,20:2026-04-06T11:32:36Z,]46:32:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-limit,7:2400000,]50:36:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-remaining,7:2370000,]60:32:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T11:32:36Z,]46:10:request-id,28:req_011CZnSiURnVDpwxVPVqXDjS,]77:25:strict-transport-security,44:max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload,]69:25:anthropic-organization-id,36:19d39eaa-efb4-49e0-afe8-a7359703719a,]23:6:Server,10:cloudflare,]40:29:x-envoy-upstream-service-time,4:1854,]27:16:Content-Encoding,4:gzip,]26:4:vary,15:Accept-Encoding,]46:13:server-timing,25:x-originResponse;dur=1864,]29:15:cf-cache-status,7:DYNAMIC,]208:10:set-cookie,189:_cfuvid=Eua5DaCG.XZKgMRVjnzqNy7rrcOjOq3GA4MPo9JTMjg-1775475156.7176938-1.0.1.1-1VtAI5EpRVu5Ar1682Swds42CB.SbzEKeRBdnzw5LBk; HttpOnly; SameSite=None; Secure; Path=/; Domain=api.anthropic.com,]73:23:Content-Security-Policy,42:default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none',]23:12:X-Robots-Tag,4:none,]33:6:CF-RAY,20:9e8079117861bdea-DUB,]]12:http_version;8:HTTP/1.1,}7:request;301407:4:path;22:/v1/messages?beta=true,9:authority;0:,6:scheme;5:https,6:method;4:POST,4:port;3:443#4:host;17:api.anthropic.com;13:timestamp_end;16:1775475156.65123^15:timestamp_start;18:1775475156.6497257^8:trailers;0:~7:content;300141:{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nThe following skills are available for use with the Skill tool:\n\n- update-config: Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\"from now on when X\", \"each time X\", \"whenever X\", \"before/after X\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so m‚Ä¶\n- simplify: Review changed code for reuse, quality, and efficiency, then fix any issues found.\n- loop: Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo, defaults to 10m) - When the user wants to set up a recurring task, poll for status, or run something repeatedly on an interval (e.g. \"check the deploy every 5 minutes\", \"keep‚Ä¶\n- claude-api: Build apps with the Claude API or Anthropic SDK.\nTRIGGER when: code imports `anthropic`/`@anthropic-ai/sdk`/`claude_agent_sdk`, or user asks to use Claude API, Anthropic SDKs, or Agent SDK.\nDO NOT TRIGGER when: code imports `openai`/other AI SDK, ge‚Ä¶\n</system-reminder>"},{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nPlan mode is active. The user indicated that they do not want you to execute yet -- you MUST NOT make any edits (with the exception of the plan file mentioned below), run any non-readonly tools (including changing configs or making commits), or otherwise make any changes to the system. This supercedes any other instructions you have received.\n\n## Plan File Info:\nNo plan file exists yet. You should create your plan at /root/.claude/plans/zippy-purring-island.md using the Write tool.\nYou should build your plan incrementally by writing to or editing this file. NOTE that this is the only file you are allowed to edit - other than this you are only allowed to take READ-ONLY actions.\n\n## Plan Workflow\n\n### Phase 1: Initial Understanding\nGoal: Gain a comprehensive understanding of the user's request by reading through code and asking them questions. Critical: In this phase you should only use the Explore subagent type.\n\n1. Focus on understanding the user's request and the code associated with their request. Actively search for existing functions, utilities, and patterns that can be reused ‚Äî avoid proposing new code when suitable implementations already exist.\n\n2. **Launch up to 3 Explore agents IN PARALLEL** (single message, multiple tool calls) to efficiently explore the codebase.\n   - Use 1 agent when the task is isolated to known files, the user provided specific file paths, or you're making a small targeted change.\n   - Use multiple agents when: the scope is uncertain, multiple areas of the codebase are involved, or you need to understand existing patterns before planning.\n   - Quality over quantity - 3 agents maximum, but you should try to use the minimum number of agents necessary (usually just 1)\n   - If using multiple agents: Provide each agent with a specific search focus or area to explore. Example: One agent searches for existing implementations, another explores related components, a third investigating testing patterns\n\n### Phase 2: Design\nGoal: Design an implementation approach.\n\nLaunch Plan agent(s) to design the implementation based on the user's intent and your exploration results from Phase 1.\n\nYou can launch up to 1 agent(s) in parallel.\n\n**Guidelines:**\n- **Default**: Launch at least 1 Plan agent for most tasks - it helps validate your understanding and consider alternatives\n- **Skip agents**: Only for truly trivial tasks (typo fixes, single-line changes, simple renames)\n\nIn the agent prompt:\n- Provide comprehensive background context from Phase 1 exploration including filenames and code path traces\n- Describe requirements and constraints\n- Request a detailed implementation plan\n\n### Phase 3: Review\nGoal: Review the plan(s) from Phase 2 and ensure alignment with the user's intentions.\n1. Read the critical files identified by agents to deepen your understanding\n2. Ensure that the plans align with the user's original request\n3. Use AskUserQuestion to clarify any remaining questions with the user\n\n### Phase 4: Final Plan\nGoal: Write your final plan to the plan file (the only file you can edit).\n- Begin with a **Context** section: explain why this change is being made ‚Äî the problem or need it addresses, what prompted it, and the intended outcome\n- Include only your recommended approach, not all alternatives\n- Ensure that the plan file is concise enough to scan quickly, but detailed enough to execute effectively\n- Include the paths of critical files to be modified\n- Reference existing functions and utilities you found that should be reused, with their file paths\n- Include a verification section describing how to test the changes end-to-end (run the code, use MCP tools, run tests)\n\n### Phase 5: Call ExitPlanMode\nAt the very end of your turn, once you have asked the user questions and are happy with your final plan file - you should always call ExitPlanMode to indicate to the user that you are done planning.\nThis is critical - your turn should only end with either using the AskUserQuestion tool OR calling ExitPlanMode. Do not stop unless it's for these 2 reasons\n\n**Important:** Use AskUserQuestion ONLY to clarify requirements or choose between approaches. Use ExitPlanMode to request plan approval. Do NOT ask about plan approval in any other way - no text questions, no AskUserQuestion. Phrases like \"Is this plan okay?\", \"Should I proceed?\", \"How does this plan look?\", \"Any changes before we start?\", or similar MUST use ExitPlanMode.\n\nNOTE: At any point in time through this workflow you should feel free to ask the user questions or clarifications using the AskUserQuestion tool. Don't make large assumptions about user intent. The goal is to present a well researched plan to the user, and tie any loose ends before implementation begins.\n</system-reminder>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nAs you answer the user's questions, you can use the following context:\n# currentDate\nToday's date is 2026-04-06.\n\n      IMPORTANT: this context may or may not be relevant to your tasks. You should not respond to this context unless it is highly relevant to your task.\n</system-reminder>\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Write tests for evaluation/usage/export_flows.py to achieve at least 80% code coverage. Read the file to understand all the functions, then write a comprehensive test suite in evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py. Use pytest with mocks for filesystem and mitmproxy dependencies. Focus on testing the pure logic functions with various inputs, edge cases, and error paths."}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C6noEDyPYZcDyUs33gUpi5","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Explore export_flows.py and surrounding codebase","subagent_type":"Explore","prompt":"Read the file at /workspace/evaluation/usage/export_flows.py in full detail. Also look at the directory structure of /workspace/evaluation/usage/ to understand what other files exist. I need to understand every function, class, import, and logic branch in export_flows.py so I can write a comprehensive test suite. Please provide:\n1. The complete content of export_flows.py\n2. The directory listing of /workspace/evaluation/usage/\n3. Any existing test files for reference (e.g., test_*.py files in that directory)\n4. Any imports or dependencies that need to be mocked (mitmproxy, filesystem operations, etc.)"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C6noEDyPYZcDyUs33gUpi5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all the information needed to provide a comprehensive analysis. Let me create a detailed response.\n\n## Comprehensive Analysis of export_flows.py\n\nI've thoroughly analyzed the file. Here's the complete information you need for writing a comprehensive test suite:\n\n### 1. **Complete File Content**\n\nThe file is located at `/workspace/export_flows.py` (1430 lines total). The complete content is shown above.\n\n### 2. **Directory Structure**\n\n```\n/workspace/\n‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ .git/\n‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ .DS_Store\n‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ export_flows.py\n```\n\nNo existing test files found. You'll be creating the first test suite.\n\n### 3. **All Functions, Classes, and Logic**\n\nHere's a complete breakdown organized by category:\n\n#### **Constants & Data Structures**\n- `SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX` (dict): Maps agent names (\"cc\", \"vix\") to system prompt array indices\n- `MODEL_PRICING` (dict): Pricing per token for 8 Claude models (input, cache_write, cache_read, output)\n- `_SORTED_PREFIXES`: Sorted model keys for longest-first matching\n- `_REDACTED_HEADERS`: Headers to redact (x-api-key, authorization)\n- `READ_TOOLS`, `WRITE_TOOLS`: Tool name sets\n- `AGENT_COLORS`: Hex colors for agents\n- `_PROJECT_ROOT`: Computed base directory\n\n#### **Utility Functions**\n\n1. **count_whitespace_stats(text)** ‚Üí dict\n   - Counts newlines, runs of 2+ spaces, total chars\n   - Returns dict with: line_returns_count, unnecessary_space_count, total_chars\n\n2. **parse_request_body(request_path)** ‚Üí dict | None\n   - Loads JSON from request.json file\n   - Returns None on JSONDecodeError\n\n3. **get_canonical_model(model_id)** ‚Üí str | None\n   - Matches model_id prefix (with date suffix) to base model\n   - Uses longest-first matching\n\n4. **get_pricing(model_id)** ‚Üí dict | None\n   - Returns pricing dict for a model or None if unknown\n\n5. **sanitize_path(path)** ‚Üí str\n   - Converts URL path to safe directory name\n   - Removes query strings, special chars\n   - Max 80 chars\n\n6. **format_headers(headers)** ‚Üí str\n   - Formats mitmproxy headers\n   - Redacts sensitive headers (x-api-key, authorization)\n\n7. **_resolve_read_file_name(name, tool_input)** ‚Üí str\n   - Maps \"read_file\" to \"read_file_compressed\" or \"read_file_uncompressed\"\n   - Based on tool_input.mode\n\n8. **_system_prompt_hash(body_json, agent_name)** ‚Üí str | None\n   - Extracts system prompt from body by agent index\n   - Returns SHA256 hash (first 12 chars)\n\n9. **_get_file_path(input_data)** ‚Üí str | None\n   - Extracts file_path or path from tool input\n   - Converts relative paths to absolute using _PROJECT_ROOT\n\n10. **_format_tool_params(input_data)** ‚Üí str\n    - Formats tool input params as compact key=value pairs\n\n11. **_agent_color(name)** ‚Üí str\n    - Returns deterministic hex color based on MD5 hash\n\n#### **Main Processing Functions**\n\n12. **write_request(flow: HTTPFlow, directory)** ‚Üí None\n    - Writes request_headers.txt (method + URL + formatted headers)\n    - Writes request.json (pretty-printed if valid JSON, else raw)\n\n13. **write_response(flow: HTTPFlow, directory)** ‚Üí None\n    - Writes response_raw.txt (status + headers + body)\n    - Returns early if no response\n\n14. **extract_stop_reason(response_raw)** ‚Üí str\n    - Extracts stop_reason from SSE message_delta events\n    - Fallback: parses JSON response\n    - Returns \"unknown\" if not found\n\n15. **redact_flow_files(directory)** ‚Üí None\n    - In-place redaction of .flow files\n    - Redacts API keys from request headers using FlowReader/FlowWriter\n\n16. **export_flows(input_dir, output_dir)** ‚Üí None\n    - Core function: exports .flow files to per-flow directories\n    - Directory structure: {agent}/{step_index}/{request_index}/\n    - Skips /count_token URLs and quota requests\n    - For \"cc\" agent: step boundary = system prompt change (checked before writing)\n    - For other agents: step boundary = end_turn stop_reason (checked after writing)\n    - Writes: request_headers.txt, request.json, response_raw.txt, timing.json\n\n17. **extract_usage(directory)** ‚Üí None\n    - Extracts token usage from SSE message_delta or JSON response\n    - Merges timing data and removes timing.json\n    - Keeps only: input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_creation_input_tokens, cache_read_input_tokens\n\n18. **extract_prompts(directory)** ‚Üí None\n    - Extracts system prompt and first user message from request.json\n    - Concatenates text blocks from system array\n    - Writes: system_prompt.md, first_user_message.md\n\n#### **Analysis Functions (Complex)**\n\n19. **extract_read_file_whitespace(body)** ‚Üí dict\n    - Analyzes whitespace stats from read_file tool results\n    - Builds tool_use_id ‚Üí tool_name map\n    - Aggregates stats from tool_result blocks\n\n20. **categorize_input_sources(body)** ‚Üí dict\n    - Categorizes input chars by tool and cache position\n    - Last user message ‚Üí cache_write\n    - Second-to-last (assistant) message ‚Üí cache_write for tool_use\n    - Everything else ‚Üí cache_read\n    - Returns: total_chars, tool_results {}, tool_calls {}\n\n21. **categorize_output_sources(response_path)** ‚Üí dict\n    - Parses SSE content_block events\n    - State machine: content_block_start ‚Üí delta ‚Üí stop\n    - Reconstructs text and tool_use blocks\n    - Fallback: non-streaming JSON parse\n    - Returns: llm_text chars, tool_calls {tool_name: chars}\n\n22. **parse_response_content(response_path)** ‚Üí list\n    - Parses response into list of content blocks\n    - Returns: [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": str}, {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": str, \"input\": dict}]\n\n23. **export_parsed_response(response_path, output_path)** ‚Üí bool\n    - Converts response_raw.txt to human-readable response_parsed.txt\n    - Text blocks output as-is\n    - Tool calls formatted as [ToolName(params)]\n\n24. **export_parsed_responses(directory)** ‚Üí None\n    - Walks directory and exports all response_parsed.txt files\n\n#### **Cost & Attribution Functions**\n\n25. **calculate_costs(directory)** ‚Üí None\n    - Computes dollar costs from usage.json + pricing\n    - Removes top-level token fields\n    - Adds canonical model to usage\n    - Stores result in usage[\"cost\"] with breakdown by: input, cache_write, cache_read, output, total\n\n26. **extract_file_ops(body, response_path)** ‚Üí dict\n    - Extracts file read/write operations\n    - Tracks per-file: calls, chars, tool_ids, file_size\n    - Returns: input {unique_files_read, total_read_chars, per_file}, output {files_written, unique_files_written, total_write_chars, per_file}\n\n27. **attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing)** ‚Üí dict\n    - Attributes tokens/cost to source categories\n    - Input: distributed proportionally by char count\n    - Output: distributed proportionally by char count\n    - Returns: by_source {input {tool_results, tool_calls}, output {llm_text, tool_calls}}\n\n28. **extract_source_attribution(directory)** ‚Üí None\n    - Combined function: calls categorize_input/output, attribute_tokens, extract_file_ops, extract_read_file_whitespace\n    - Enriches usage.json with: by_source, read_file_whitespace, file_ops\n\n#### **Aggregation & Summary Functions**\n\n29. **_aggregate_by_source(agg, flow_by_source)** ‚Üí None\n    - Aggregates per-flow by_source into summary (mutates agg)\n    - Sums tokens/dollars for input and output\n\n30. **_round_by_source(agg)** ‚Üí None\n    - Rounds dollar values to 6 decimals (mutates agg)\n\n31. **_finalize_file_ops(fops)** ‚Üí None\n    - Nested function in summarize_usage\n    - Converts tool_ids maps to calls/chars\n    - Recomputes scalars\n\n32. **_finalize_timing(bucket)** ‚Üí None\n    - Nested function in summarize_usage\n    - Computes wall_clock_ms and avg_duration_ms\n\n33. **summarize_usage(directory)** ‚Üí None\n    - Most complex function: aggregates per-request usage into summary per agent\n    - Creates buckets by: model, step, total\n    - Aggregates: cost, timing, whitespace, by_source, file_ops\n    - Writes usage.json to agent_dir root\n\n34. **main()** ‚Üí None\n    - Entry point: orchestrates pipeline\n    - Calls: redact_flow_files ‚Üí export_flows ‚Üí extract_usage ‚Üí export_parsed_responses ‚Üí extract_prompts ‚Üí calculate_costs ‚Üí extract_source_attribution ‚Üí summarize_usage\n\n### 4. **Critical Dependencies to Mock**\n\n```python\n# mitmproxy imports (external library - will need mocking)\nfrom mitmproxy.io import FlowReader, FlowWriter\nfrom mitmproxy.exceptions import FlowReadException\nfrom mitmproxy.http import HTTPFlow\n\n# Standard library (mostly file I/O and JSON)\nimport argparse, glob, hashlib, json, os, re, shutil\n```\n\n**Key mocking targets:**\n- `FlowReader` / `FlowWriter` - streams binary .flow files\n- `HTTPFlow` - mitmproxy flow object with `.request` and `.response` attributes\n- File system operations: `open()`, `os.path.exists()`, `os.makedirs()`, `os.walk()`, `shutil.rmtree()`, `os.remove()`, `os.listdir()`, `os.path.getsize()`\n- `glob.glob()` - file pattern matching\n\n### 5. **Logic Branches & Edge Cases**\n\n**Key conditional paths:**\n1. Step boundary detection (cc vs vix agents - different logic)\n2. SSE streaming vs non-streaming response parsing (dual parsers)\n3. Tool name resolution (read_file ‚Üí read_file_compressed/uncompressed)\n4. Cache positioning logic (last user msg, second-to-last assistant msg)\n5. Error handling: FlowReadException, JSONDecodeError, OSError, ValueError\n6. File existence checks and graceful fallbacks\n7. Division by zero checks in proportional distribution (total_chars, total_output_chars)\n\n**Major data transformations:**\n- Flow objects ‚Üí directory hierarchy with text files\n- Raw response ‚Üí parsed content blocks (SSE state machine)\n- Token usage + character counts ‚Üí cost attribution\n- Per-request metrics ‚Üí per-agent summaries with model/step breakdowns\n\nThis comprehensive breakdown should give you everything needed to write tests covering all functions, edge cases, and integration points."}]}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Let me read the actual file content to get precise details."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015avzr8M5VNPKV6vBAgi4VC","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/evaluation/usage/export_flows.py"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"File does not exist. Note: your current working directory is /workspace.","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_015avzr8M5VNPKV6vBAgi4VC"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012u255NKAAEzeroAegFSZ3j","name":"Glob","input":{"pattern":"**/export_flows.py"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012u255NKAAEzeroAegFSZ3j","type":"tool_result","content":"export_flows.py"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VXQnWASKFjMpV1XTsZY25z","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/export_flows.py"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VXQnWASKFjMpV1XTsZY25z","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"Export mitmproxy flow files into per-flow directories with request.json, request_headers.txt, and response_raw.txt.\"\"\"\n3\t\n4\timport argparse\n5\timport glob\n6\timport hashlib\n7\timport json\n8\timport os\n9\timport re\n10\timport shutil\n11\tfrom mitmproxy.io import FlowReader, FlowWriter\n12\tfrom mitmproxy.exceptions import FlowReadException\n13\tfrom mitmproxy.http import HTTPFlow\n14\t\n15\tSYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX = {\n16\t    \"cc\": 2,\n17\t    \"vix\": 0,\n18\t}\n19\t\n20\tMODEL_PRICING = {\n21\t    \"claude-opus-4-6\":   {\"input\": 5e-6,    \"cache_write\": 6.25e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.50e-6,  \"output\": 25e-6},\n22\t    \"claude-opus-4-5\":   {\"input\": 5e-6,    \"cache_write\": 6.25e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.50e-6,  \"output\": 25e-6},\n23\t    \"claude-opus-4-1\":   {\"input\": 15e-6,   \"cache_write\": 18.75e-6, \"cache_read\": 1.50e-6,  \"output\": 75e-6},\n24\t    \"claude-opus-4\":     {\"input\": 15e-6,   \"cache_write\": 18.75e-6, \"cache_read\": 1.50e-6,  \"output\": 75e-6},\n25\t    \"claude-sonnet-4-6\": {\"input\": 3e-6,    \"cache_write\": 3.75e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.30e-6,  \"output\": 15e-6},\n26\t    \"claude-sonnet-4-5\": {\"input\": 3e-6,    \"cache_write\": 3.75e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.30e-6,  \"output\": 15e-6},\n27\t    \"claude-sonnet-4\":   {\"input\": 3e-6,    \"cache_write\": 3.75e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.30e-6,  \"output\": 15e-6},\n28\t    \"claude-haiku-4-5\":  {\"input\": 1e-6,    \"cache_write\": 1.25e-6,  \"cache_read\": 0.10e-6,  \"output\": 5e-6},\n29\t    \"claude-haiku-3-5\":  {\"input\": 0.80e-6, \"cache_write\": 1e-6,     \"cache_read\": 0.08e-6,  \"output\": 4e-6},\n30\t}\n31\t\n32\t# Sort prefixes longest-first so \"claude-opus-4-5\" matches before \"claude-opus-4\"\n33\t_SORTED_PREFIXES = sorted(MODEL_PRICING.keys(), key=len, reverse=True)\n34\t\n35\t\n36\tdef count_whitespace_stats(text):\n37\t    \"\"\"Count line returns and unnecessary spaces in text.\n38\t\n39\t    Returns dict with:\n40\t      - line_returns_count: number of \\\\n characters\n41\t      - unnecessary_space_count: for each run of 2+ spaces, count len(run) - 1\n42\t      - total_chars: total character count of the text\n43\t    \"\"\"\n44\t    line_returns = text.count(\"\\n\")\n45\t    unnecessary_spaces = sum(len(m) - 1 for m in re.findall(r\" {2,}\", text))\n46\t    return {\n47\t        \"line_returns_count\": line_returns,\n48\t        \"unnecessary_space_count\": unnecessary_spaces,\n49\t        \"total_chars\": len(text),\n50\t    }\n51\t\n52\t\n53\tdef parse_request_body(request_path: str):\n54\t    \"\"\"Parse the JSON body from a request.json file. Returns the parsed dict or None.\"\"\"\n55\t    try:\n56\t        with open(request_path, \"r\") as f:\n57\t            return json.load(f)\n58\t    except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n59\t        return None\n60\t\n61\t\n62\tdef get_canonical_model(model_id: str):\n63\t    \"\"\"Return the canonical model name (without date suffix) or None if unknown.\"\"\"\n64\t    for prefix in _SORTED_PREFIXES:\n65\t        if model_id.startswith(prefix):\n66\t            return prefix\n67\t    return None\n68\t\n69\t\n70\tdef get_pricing(model_id: str):\n71\t    \"\"\"Match a model ID (possibly with date suffix) to pricing. Returns pricing dict or None.\"\"\"\n72\t    canonical = get_canonical_model(model_id)\n73\t    if canonical:\n74\t        return MODEL_PRICING[canonical]\n75\t    return None\n76\t\n77\t\n78\tdef sanitize_path(path: str) -> str:\n79\t    \"\"\"Turn a URL path into a safe directory name component.\"\"\"\n80\t    path = path.split(\"?\")[0]\n81\t    path = path.replace(\"/\", \"_\")\n82\t    path = path.strip(\"_\")\n83\t    path = re.sub(r\"[^a-zA-Z0-9_\\-]\", \"\", path)\n84\t    return path[:80]\n85\t\n86\t\n87\t_REDACTED_HEADERS = {b\"x-api-key\", b\"authorization\"}\n88\t\n89\t\n90\tdef format_headers(headers) -> str:\n91\t    lines = []\n92\t    for k, v in headers.fields:\n93\t        if k.lower() in _REDACTED_HEADERS:\n94\t            lines.append(f\"{k}: [REDACTED]\")\n95\t        else:\n96\t            lines.append(f\"{k}: {v}\")\n97\t    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n98\t\n99\t\n100\tdef write_request(flow: HTTPFlow, directory: str):\n101\t    req = flow.request\n102\t    # Write headers file (method+URL line, blank line, headers)\n103\t    header_lines = [\n104\t        f\"{req.method} {req.pretty_url}\",\n105\t        \"\",\n106\t        format_headers(req.headers),\n107\t    ]\n108\t    with open(os.path.join(directory, \"request_headers.txt\"), \"w\") as f:\n109\t        f.write(\"\\n\".join(header_lines))\n110\t    # Write body as JSON (pretty-printed if valid JSON, raw fallback)\n111\t    body = req.get_text(strict=False)\n112\t    if body:\n113\t        try:\n114\t            parsed = json.loads(body)\n115\t            body_out = json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n116\t        except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n117\t            body_out = body\n118\t        with open(os.path.join(directory, \"request.json\"), \"w\") as f:\n119\t            f.write(body_out)\n120\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n121\t\n122\t\n123\t\n124\tdef write_response(flow: HTTPFlow, directory: str):\n125\t    resp = flow.response\n126\t    if resp is None:\n127\t        return\n128\t    lines = [\n129\t        f\"{resp.status_code} {resp.reason}\",\n130\t        \"\",\n131\t        format_headers(resp.headers),\n132\t    ]\n133\t    body = resp.get_text(strict=False)\n134\t    if body:\n135\t        lines += [\"\", body]\n136\t    with open(os.path.join(directory, \"response_raw.txt\"), \"w\") as f:\n137\t        f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n138\t\n139\t\n140\tdef extract_stop_reason(response_raw: str) -> str:\n141\t    \"\"\"Extract stop_reason from SSE message_delta event or non-streaming JSON response.\"\"\"\n142\t    # Try SSE streaming format\n143\t    for line in response_raw.splitlines():\n144\t        line = line.strip()\n145\t        if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n146\t            continue\n147\t        payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n148\t        if '\"type\":\"message_delta\"' not in payload and '\"type\": \"message_delta\"' not in payload:\n149\t            continue\n150\t        try:\n151\t            data = json.loads(payload)\n152\t            delta = data.get(\"delta\", {})\n153\t            reason = delta.get(\"stop_reason\")\n154\t            if reason:\n155\t                return reason\n156\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n157\t            continue\n158\t\n159\t    # Fallback: non-streaming JSON response\n160\t    for line in reversed(response_raw.splitlines()):\n161\t        line = line.strip()\n162\t        if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n163\t            continue\n164\t        try:\n165\t            data = json.loads(line)\n166\t            if data.get(\"type\") == \"message\":\n167\t                reason = data.get(\"stop_reason\")\n168\t                if reason:\n169\t                    return reason\n170\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n171\t            continue\n172\t\n173\t    return \"unknown\"\n174\t\n175\t\n176\tdef redact_flow_files(directory: str):\n177\t    \"\"\"Redact sensitive headers (API keys) from .flow files in-place.\"\"\"\n178\t    flow_files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(directory, \"*.flow\")))\n179\t    if not flow_files:\n180\t        return\n181\t\n182\t    count = 0\n183\t    for filepath in flow_files:\n184\t        flows = []\n185\t        modified = False\n186\t        try:\n187\t            with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:\n188\t                reader = FlowReader(f)\n189\t                for flow in reader.stream():\n190\t                    if isinstance(flow, HTTPFlow):\n191\t                        for header in _REDACTED_HEADERS:\n192\t                            if flow.request.headers.get(header):\n193\t                                flow.request.headers[header] = \"[REDACTED]\"\n194\t                                modified = True\n195\t                    flows.append(flow)\n196\t        except (FlowReadException, Exception) as e:\n197\t            print(f\"  Skipping {os.path.basename(filepath)}: {e}\")\n198\t            continue\n199\t\n200\t        if modified:\n201\t            with open(filepath, \"wb\") as f:\n202\t                writer = FlowWriter(f)\n203\t                for flow in flows:\n204\t                    writer.add(flow)\n205\t            count += 1\n206\t\n207\t    print(f\"\\nRedacted API keys in {count} flow files\")\n208\t\n209\t\n210\tdef _system_prompt_hash(body_json, agent_name):\n211\t    \"\"\"Return a short hash of the relevant system prompt, or None.\"\"\"\n212\t    system = body_json.get(\"system\")\n213\t    if not system:\n214\t        return None\n215\t    index = SYSTEM_PROMPT_INDEX.get(agent_name, 0)\n216\t    if index >= len(system):\n217\t        return None\n218\t    text = system[index].get(\"text\", \"\")\n219\t    if not text:\n220\t        return None\n221\t    return hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest()[:12]\n222\t\n223\t\n224\tdef export_flows(input_dir: str, output_dir: str):\n225\t    \"\"\"Export .flow files from input_dir into per-flow directories under output_dir.\n226\t\n227\t    Directory structure: {agent}/{step_index}/{request_index}/\n228\t    Steps are delimited by end_turn stop_reason in responses.\n229\t    \"\"\"\n230\t    flow_files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(input_dir, \"*.flow\")))\n231\t    if not flow_files:\n232\t        print(f\"No *.flow files found in {input_dir}\")\n233\t        return\n234\t\n235\t    total = 0\n236\t    for filepath in flow_files:\n237\t        filename = os.path.basename(filepath)\n238\t        name = os.path.splitext(filename)[0]\n239\t        file_dir = os.path.join(output_dir, name)\n240\t        if os.path.exists(file_dir):\n241\t            shutil.rmtree(file_dir)\n242\t        os.makedirs(file_dir)\n243\t        print(f\"Reading {filename}...\")\n244\t        try:\n245\t            step_index = 1\n246\t            request_index = 1\n247\t            prev_prompt_hash = None\n248\t            with open(filepath, \"rb\") as f:\n249\t                reader = FlowReader(f)\n250\t                for flow in reader.stream():\n251\t                    if not isinstance(flow, HTTPFlow):\n252\t                        continue\n253\t\n254\t                    url = flow.request.pretty_url\n255\t                    if \"/count_token\" in url:\n256\t                        continue\n257\t\n258\t                    # Parse body to check for quota requests\n259\t                    body_text = flow.request.get_text(strict=False)\n260\t                    body_json = None\n261\t                    if body_text:\n262\t                        try:\n263\t                            body_json = json.loads(body_text)\n264\t                            messages = body_json.get(\"messages\", [])\n265\t                            system = body_json.get(\"system\")\n266\t                            if messages and not system:\n267\t                                first_msg = messages[0]\n268\t                                content = first_msg.get(\"content\", \"\")\n269\t                                if isinstance(content, str) and content == \"quota\":\n270\t                                    continue\n271\t                        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n272\t                            pass\n273\t\n274\t                    # For cc: step boundary = system prompt change (checked before writing)\n275\t                    if name == \"cc\" and body_json is not None:\n276\t                        prompt_hash = _system_prompt_hash(body_json, name)\n277\t                        if prompt_hash is not None and prev_prompt_hash is not None and prompt_hash != prev_prompt_hash:\n278\t                            step_index += 1\n279\t                            request_index = 1\n280\t                        if prompt_hash is not None:\n281\t                            prev_prompt_hash = prompt_hash\n282\t\n283\t                    flow_dir = os.path.join(file_dir, str(step_index), str(request_index))\n284\t                    os.makedirs(flow_dir, exist_ok=True)\n285\t\n286\t                    write_request(flow, flow_dir)\n287\t                    write_response(flow, flow_dir)\n288\t                    # Write timing data inline\n289\t                    timing = {}\n290\t                    if flow.request:\n291\t                        timing[\"request_start\"] = flow.request.timestamp_start\n292\t                    if flow.response:\n293\t                        timing[\"response_end\"] = flow.response.timestamp_end\n294\t                    with open(os.path.join(flow_dir, \"timing.json\"), \"w\") as f:\n295\t                        json.dump(timing, f, indent=2)\n296\t                        f.write(\"\\n\")\n297\t\n298\t                    # Extract stop_reason to determine step boundaries\n299\t                    response_raw = \"\"\n300\t                    resp = flow.response\n301\t                    if resp is not None:\n302\t                        response_raw = resp.get_text(strict=False) or \"\"\n303\t                    stop_reason = extract_stop_reason(response_raw)\n304\t\n305\t                    print(f\"  [step {step_index}, req {request_index}] {flow.request.method} {flow.request.pretty_url} ({stop_reason})\")\n306\t\n307\t                    # For vix: step boundary = end_turn stop_reason (checked after writing)\n308\t                    if name != \"cc\":\n309\t                        if stop_reason == \"end_turn\":\n310\t                            step_index += 1\n311\t                            request_index = 1\n312\t                        else:\n313\t                            request_index += 1\n314\t                    else:\n315\t                        request_index += 1\n316\t\n317\t                    total += 1\n318\t        except FlowReadException as e:\n319\t            print(f\"  Skipping {filename}: {e}\")\n320\t        except Exception as e:\n321\t            print(f\"  Skipping {filename}: {e}\")\n322\t\n323\t    print(f\"\\nExported {total} flows to {output_dir}\")\n324\t\n325\t\n326\tdef extract_usage(directory: str):\n327\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, extract token usage from SSE message_delta events into usage.json.\"\"\"\n328\t    count = 0\n329\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n330\t        if \"response_raw.txt\" not in filenames:\n331\t            continue\n332\t\n333\t        response_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\")\n334\t        usage = None\n335\t        with open(response_path, \"r\") as f:\n336\t            content = f.read()\n337\t\n338\t        # Try SSE streaming format: look for message_delta events\n339\t        for line in content.splitlines():\n340\t            line = line.strip()\n341\t            if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n342\t                continue\n343\t            payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n344\t            if '\"type\":\"message_delta\"' not in payload and '\"type\": \"message_delta\"' not in payload:\n345\t                continue\n346\t            try:\n347\t                data = json.loads(payload)\n348\t                usage = data.get(\"usage\")\n349\t            except json.JSONDecodeError:\n350\t                continue\n351\t\n352\t        # Fallback: non-streaming JSON response (single message object)\n353\t        # The body comes after a blank line following the headers\n354\t        if usage is None:\n355\t            # Find the last {...\"type\":\"message\"...} JSON in the content\n356\t            for line in reversed(content.splitlines()):\n357\t                line = line.strip()\n358\t                if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n359\t                    continue\n360\t                try:\n361\t                    msg = json.loads(line)\n362\t                    if msg.get(\"type\") == \"message\" and \"usage\" in msg:\n363\t                        usage = msg[\"usage\"]\n364\t                        break\n365\t                except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n366\t                    continue\n367\t\n368\t        if usage is None:\n369\t            print(f\"  Warning: no usage found in {response_path}\")\n370\t            continue\n371\t\n372\t        # Keep only the token count fields we need\n373\t        TOKEN_FIELDS = (\"input_tokens\", \"output_tokens\", \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", \"cache_read_input_tokens\")\n374\t        usage = {k: v for k, v in usage.items() if k in TOKEN_FIELDS}\n375\t\n376\t        # Merge timing data if available\n377\t        timing_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"timing.json\")\n378\t        if os.path.exists(timing_path):\n379\t            with open(timing_path, \"r\") as f:\n380\t                timing = json.load(f)\n381\t            request_start = timing.get(\"request_start\")\n382\t            response_end = timing.get(\"response_end\")\n383\t            timing_block = {}\n384\t            if request_start:\n385\t                timing_block[\"request_start\"] = request_start\n386\t            if response_end:\n387\t                timing_block[\"response_end\"] = response_end\n388\t            if request_start and response_end:\n389\t                timing_block[\"duration_ms\"] = round((response_end - request_start) * 1000)\n390\t            if timing_block:\n391\t                usage[\"timing\"] = timing_block\n392\t            os.remove(timing_path)\n393\t\n394\t        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n395\t        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n396\t            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n397\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n398\t        count += 1\n399\t\n400\t    print(f\"\\nExtracted usage for {count} flows\")\n401\t\n402\t\n403\t\n404\tdef extract_prompts(directory: str):\n405\t    \"\"\"Extract system prompt and first user message from request.json files into per-request markdown files.\"\"\"\n406\t    count = 0\n407\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n408\t        if \"request.json\" not in filenames:\n409\t            continue\n410\t\n411\t        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n412\t\n413\t        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n414\t        if body is None:\n415\t            print(f\"  Warning: no JSON body found in {request_path}\")\n416\t            continue\n417\t\n418\t        # System prompt: concatenate all text blocks from body[\"system\"]\n419\t        system = body.get(\"system\")\n420\t        if system and isinstance(system, list):\n421\t            texts = [block.get(\"text\", \"\") for block in system if block.get(\"type\") == \"text\"]\n422\t            system_text = \"\\n\\n\".join(t for t in texts if t)\n423\t            if system_text:\n424\t                with open(os.path.join(dirpath, \"system_prompt.md\"), \"w\") as f:\n425\t                    f.write(system_text)\n426\t\n427\t        # First user message: find first message with role==\"user\", concatenate text blocks\n428\t        messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n429\t        for msg in messages:\n430\t            if msg.get(\"role\") == \"user\":\n431\t                content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n432\t                if isinstance(content, list):\n433\t                    texts = [block.get(\"text\", \"\") for block in content if block.get(\"type\") == \"text\"]\n434\t                    user_text = \"\\n\\n\".join(t for t in texts if t)\n435\t                    if user_text:\n436\t                        with open(os.path.join(dirpath, \"first_user_message.md\"), \"w\") as f:\n437\t                            f.write(user_text)\n438\t                break\n439\t\n440\t        count += 1\n441\t\n442\t    print(f\"\\nExtracted prompts for {count} requests\")\n443\t\n444\t\n445\t\n446\tdef _resolve_read_file_name(name, tool_input):\n447\t    \"\"\"Resolve read_file tool name to compressed/uncompressed variant.\"\"\"\n448\t    if name == \"read_file\":\n449\t        mode = tool_input.get(\"mode\", \"original\") if isinstance(tool_input, dict) else \"original\"\n450\t        return \"read_file_compressed\" if mode == \"compress\" else \"read_file_uncompressed\"\n451\t    return name\n452\t\n453\t\n454\tdef extract_read_file_whitespace(body):\n455\t    \"\"\"Extract whitespace stats from read_file/Read tool results in the request body.\"\"\"\n456\t    ws = {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n457\t\n458\t    # Build tool_use_id -> tool_name map from assistant messages\n459\t    tool_id_to_name = {}\n460\t    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n461\t    for msg in messages:\n462\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n463\t            continue\n464\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n465\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n466\t            continue\n467\t        for block in content:\n468\t            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n469\t                tool_id_to_name[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = _resolve_read_file_name(\n470\t                    block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n471\t\n472\t    for msg in messages:\n473\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n474\t            continue\n475\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n476\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n477\t            continue\n478\t        for block in content:\n479\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n480\t                continue\n481\t            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n482\t            tool_name = tool_id_to_name.get(tool_use_id, \"unknown\")\n483\t            if not (tool_name.startswith(\"read_file\") or tool_name == \"Read\"):\n484\t                continue\n485\t            result_content = block.get(\"content\", \"\")\n486\t            if isinstance(result_content, str):\n487\t                text_for_ws = result_content\n488\t            elif isinstance(result_content, list):\n489\t                text_for_ws = \"\".join(b.get(\"text\", \"\") for b in result_content)\n490\t            else:\n491\t                text_for_ws = \"\"\n492\t            stats = count_whitespace_stats(text_for_ws)\n493\t            for k in (\"line_returns_count\", \"unnecessary_space_count\", \"total_chars\"):\n494\t                ws[k] += stats[k]\n495\t\n496\t    return ws\n497\t\n498\t\n499\tdef categorize_input_sources(body):\n500\t    \"\"\"Count input characters from tool results and tool use blocks, split by cache position.\n501\t\n502\t    Returns: {\n503\t        \"total_chars\": int,  # total chars of entire request body\n504\t        \"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 1234}, ...},\n505\t        \"tool_calls\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 567}, ...},\n506\t    }\n507\t\n508\t    Position logic:\n509\t    - Last user message content ‚Üí cache_write (new content being written to cache)\n510\t    - Second-to-last message (assistant before last user) ‚Üí cache_write for tool_use blocks\n511\t    - Everything else ‚Üí cache_read\n512\t    \"\"\"\n513\t    total_chars = len(json.dumps(body))\n514\t    tool_results = {}\n515\t    tool_calls = {}\n516\t\n517\t    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n518\t\n519\t    # Find last user message index and second-to-last message index\n520\t    last_user_idx = -1\n521\t    for i in range(len(messages) - 1, -1, -1):\n522\t        if messages[i].get(\"role\") == \"user\":\n523\t            last_user_idx = i\n524\t            break\n525\t    second_to_last_idx = last_user_idx - 1 if last_user_idx > 0 else -1\n526\t\n527\t    # Build tool_use_id -> tool_name map from assistant messages\n528\t    tool_id_to_name = {}\n529\t    for msg in messages:\n530\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n531\t            continue\n532\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n533\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n534\t            continue\n535\t        for block in content:\n536\t            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n537\t                tool_id_to_name[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = _resolve_read_file_name(\n538\t                    block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n539\t\n540\t    # Collect tool_result chars from user messages\n541\t    for i, msg in enumerate(messages):\n542\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n543\t            continue\n544\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n545\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n546\t            continue\n547\t        is_cache_write = (i == last_user_idx)\n548\t        for block in content:\n549\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n550\t                continue\n551\t            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n552\t            tool_name = tool_id_to_name.get(tool_use_id, \"unknown\")\n553\t            chars = len(json.dumps(block))\n554\t            if tool_name not in tool_results:\n555\t                tool_results[tool_name] = {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 0}\n556\t            if is_cache_write:\n557\t                tool_results[tool_name][\"cache_write_chars\"] += chars\n558\t            else:\n559\t                tool_results[tool_name][\"cache_read_chars\"] += chars\n560\t\n561\t    # Collect tool_use chars from assistant messages\n562\t    for i, msg in enumerate(messages):\n563\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n564\t            continue\n565\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n566\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n567\t            continue\n568\t        is_cache_write = (i == second_to_last_idx)\n569\t        for block in content:\n570\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_use\":\n571\t                continue\n572\t            tool_name = _resolve_read_file_name(\n573\t                block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n574\t            chars = len(json.dumps(block))\n575\t            if tool_name not in tool_calls:\n576\t                tool_calls[tool_name] = {\"cache_write_chars\": 0, \"cache_read_chars\": 0}\n577\t            if is_cache_write:\n578\t                tool_calls[tool_name][\"cache_write_chars\"] += chars\n579\t            else:\n580\t                tool_calls[tool_name][\"cache_read_chars\"] += chars\n581\t\n582\t    return {\"total_chars\": total_chars, \"tool_results\": tool_results, \"tool_calls\": tool_calls}\n583\t\n584\t\n585\tdef categorize_output_sources(response_path):\n586\t    \"\"\"Count output characters from the actual response (SSE stream or single JSON).\n587\t\n588\t    Parses content_block_start/delta/stop events from response_raw.txt.\n589\t    Returns: {\"llm_text\": int, \"tool_calls\": {\"ToolName\": int, ...}}\n590\t    \"\"\"\n591\t    llm_text_chars = 0\n592\t    tool_calls = {}\n593\t\n594\t    with open(response_path, \"r\") as f:\n595\t        content = f.read()\n596\t\n597\t    # State machine for SSE content blocks\n598\t    # blocks[index] = {\"type\": \"text\"|\"tool_use\", \"name\": str, \"text\": str, \"json\": str}\n599\t    blocks = {}\n600\t    found_sse = False\n601\t\n602\t    for line in content.splitlines():\n603\t        line = line.strip()\n604\t        if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n605\t            continue\n606\t        payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n607\t        try:\n608\t            data = json.loads(payload)\n609\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n610\t            continue\n611\t\n612\t        event_type = data.get(\"type\", \"\")\n613\t\n614\t        if event_type == \"content_block_start\":\n615\t            found_sse = True\n616\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n617\t            cb = data.get(\"content_block\", {})\n618\t            blocks[idx] = {\n619\t                \"type\": cb.get(\"type\", \"\"),\n620\t                \"name\": cb.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"),\n621\t                \"text\": \"\",\n622\t                \"json\": \"\",\n623\t            }\n624\t\n625\t        elif event_type == \"content_block_delta\":\n626\t            found_sse = True\n627\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n628\t            delta = data.get(\"delta\", {})\n629\t            delta_type = delta.get(\"type\", \"\")\n630\t            if idx in blocks:\n631\t                if delta_type == \"text_delta\":\n632\t                    blocks[idx][\"text\"] += delta.get(\"text\", \"\")\n633\t                elif delta_type == \"input_json_delta\":\n634\t                    blocks[idx][\"json\"] += delta.get(\"partial_json\", \"\")\n635\t\n636\t        elif event_type == \"content_block_stop\":\n637\t            found_sse = True\n638\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n639\t            if idx in blocks:\n640\t                block = blocks[idx]\n641\t                if block[\"type\"] == \"text\":\n642\t                    llm_text_chars += len(block[\"text\"])\n643\t                elif block[\"type\"] == \"tool_use\":\n644\t                    try:\n645\t                        input_data = json.loads(block[\"json\"]) if block[\"json\"] else {}\n646\t                    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n647\t                        input_data = {}\n648\t                    tool_name = _resolve_read_file_name(block[\"name\"], input_data)\n649\t                    # Reconstruct full block to count all chars (id, name, type, input)\n650\t                    full_block = {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": block[\"name\"], \"input\": input_data}\n651\t                    chars = len(json.dumps(full_block))\n652\t                    tool_calls[tool_name] = tool_calls.get(tool_name, 0) + chars\n653\t                del blocks[idx]\n654\t\n655\t    # Non-streaming fallback: parse single JSON message\n656\t    if not found_sse:\n657\t        for line in reversed(content.splitlines()):\n658\t            line = line.strip()\n659\t            if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n660\t                continue\n661\t            try:\n662\t                msg = json.loads(line)\n663\t                if msg.get(\"type\") != \"message\":\n664\t                    continue\n665\t                for block in msg.get(\"content\", []):\n666\t                    btype = block.get(\"type\", \"\")\n667\t                    if btype == \"text\":\n668\t                        llm_text_chars += len(block.get(\"text\", \"\"))\n669\t                    elif btype == \"tool_use\":\n670\t                        tool_name = _resolve_read_file_name(\n671\t                            block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n672\t                        chars = len(json.dumps(block))\n673\t                        tool_calls[tool_name] = tool_calls.get(tool_name, 0) + chars\n674\t                break\n675\t            except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n676\t                continue\n677\t\n678\t    return {\"llm_text\": llm_text_chars, \"tool_calls\": tool_calls}\n679\t\n680\t\n681\tdef _format_tool_params(input_data):\n682\t    \"\"\"Format tool input as compact param=value pairs.\"\"\"\n683\t    parts = []\n684\t    for key, value in input_data.items():\n685\t        if isinstance(value, str):\n686\t            parts.append(f'{key}=\"{value}\"')\n687\t        else:\n688\t            parts.append(f\"{key}={json.dumps(value)}\")\n689\t    return \", \".join(parts)\n690\t\n691\t\n692\tdef parse_response_content(response_path):\n693\t    \"\"\"Parse response_raw.txt into a list of content blocks.\n694\t\n695\t    Returns: list of {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": str} or {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": str, \"input\": dict}\n696\t    \"\"\"\n697\t    with open(response_path, \"r\") as f:\n698\t        content = f.read()\n699\t\n700\t    # SSE streaming parse\n701\t    blocks = {}\n702\t    finished = []\n703\t    found_sse = False\n704\t\n705\t    for line in content.splitlines():\n706\t        line = line.strip()\n707\t        if not line.startswith(\"data: \"):\n708\t            continue\n709\t        payload = line[len(\"data: \"):].strip()\n710\t        try:\n711\t            data = json.loads(payload)\n712\t        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n713\t            continue\n714\t\n715\t        event_type = data.get(\"type\", \"\")\n716\t\n717\t        if event_type == \"content_block_start\":\n718\t            found_sse = True\n719\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n720\t            cb = data.get(\"content_block\", {})\n721\t            blocks[idx] = {\n722\t                \"type\": cb.get(\"type\", \"\"),\n723\t                \"name\": cb.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"),\n724\t                \"text\": \"\",\n725\t                \"json\": \"\",\n726\t            }\n727\t\n728\t        elif event_type == \"content_block_delta\":\n729\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n730\t            delta = data.get(\"delta\", {})\n731\t            delta_type = delta.get(\"type\", \"\")\n732\t            if idx in blocks:\n733\t                if delta_type == \"text_delta\":\n734\t                    blocks[idx][\"text\"] += delta.get(\"text\", \"\")\n735\t                elif delta_type == \"input_json_delta\":\n736\t                    blocks[idx][\"json\"] += delta.get(\"partial_json\", \"\")\n737\t\n738\t        elif event_type == \"content_block_stop\":\n739\t            idx = data.get(\"index\", 0)\n740\t            if idx in blocks:\n741\t                block = blocks[idx]\n742\t                if block[\"type\"] == \"text\":\n743\t                    finished.append({\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": block[\"text\"]})\n744\t                elif block[\"type\"] == \"tool_use\":\n745\t                    try:\n746\t                        input_data = json.loads(block[\"json\"]) if block[\"json\"] else {}\n747\t                    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n748\t                        input_data = {}\n749\t                    finished.append({\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": block[\"name\"], \"input\": input_data})\n750\t                del blocks[idx]\n751\t\n752\t    # Non-streaming fallback\n753\t    if not found_sse:\n754\t        for line in reversed(content.splitlines()):\n755\t            line = line.strip()\n756\t            if not line.startswith(\"{\"):\n757\t                continue\n758\t            try:\n759\t                msg = json.loads(line)\n760\t                if msg.get(\"type\") != \"message\":\n761\t                    continue\n762\t                for block in msg.get(\"content\", []):\n763\t                    btype = block.get(\"type\", \"\")\n764\t                    if btype == \"text\":\n765\t                        finished.append({\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": block.get(\"text\", \"\")})\n766\t                    elif btype == \"tool_use\":\n767\t                        finished.append({\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": block.get(\"name\", \"unknown\"), \"input\": block.get(\"input\", {})})\n768\t                break\n769\t            except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n770\t                continue\n771\t\n772\t    return finished\n773\t\n774\t\n775\tdef export_parsed_response(response_path, output_path):\n776\t    \"\"\"Parse response_raw.txt and write a human-readable response_parsed.txt.\n777\t\n778\t    Text blocks are output as-is. Tool calls are displayed inline with params.\n779\t    \"\"\"\n780\t    blocks = parse_response_content(response_path)\n781\t    if not blocks:\n782\t        return False\n783\t\n784\t    lines = []\n785\t    for block in blocks:\n786\t        if block[\"type\"] == \"text\":\n787\t            lines.append(block[\"text\"])\n788\t        elif block[\"type\"] == \"tool_use\":\n789\t            params = _format_tool_params(block[\"input\"])\n790\t            lines.append(f'\\n[{block[\"name\"]}({params})]\\n')\n791\t\n792\t    with open(output_path, \"w\") as f:\n793\t        f.write(\"\".join(lines))\n794\t    return True\n795\t\n796\t\n797\tdef export_parsed_responses(directory: str):\n798\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, export response_parsed.txt for each response_raw.txt.\"\"\"\n799\t    count = 0\n800\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n801\t        if \"response_raw.txt\" not in filenames:\n802\t            continue\n803\t\n804\t        response_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\")\n805\t        output_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_parsed.txt\")\n806\t\n807\t        if export_parsed_response(response_path, output_path):\n808\t            count += 1\n809\t\n810\t    print(f\"\\nExported parsed responses for {count} flows\")\n811\t\n812\t\n813\tdef attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing):\n814\t    \"\"\"Attribute tokens/cost to source categories.\n815\t\n816\t    Input side: raw character counts per tool (no token/cost distribution ‚Äî flawed due to caching).\n817\t    Output side: proportional token/cost distribution (valid since output isn't cached).\n818\t    \"\"\"\n819\t    by_source = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n820\t\n821\t    # Input: distribute input tokens proportionally using total_chars as denominator\n822\t    cost_data = usage.get(\"cost\", {})\n823\t    _ci = cost_data.get(\"input\", {})\n824\t    _cw = cost_data.get(\"cache_write\", {})\n825\t    _cr = cost_data.get(\"cache_read\", {})\n826\t    input_tokens = _ci.get(\"tokens\", 0) + _cw.get(\"tokens\", 0) + _cr.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n827\t\n828\t    total_chars = input_sources.get(\"total_chars\", 0)\n829\t\n830\t    def _attribute_input_tool(tool_char_dict):\n831\t        \"\"\"Compute tokens/dollars/chars for a tool given its {cache_write_chars, cache_read_chars}.\"\"\"\n832\t        cw_chars = tool_char_dict.get(\"cache_write_chars\", 0)\n833\t        cr_chars = tool_char_dict.get(\"cache_read_chars\", 0)\n834\t        cw_tokens = round(input_tokens * (cw_chars / total_chars))\n835\t        cr_tokens = round(input_tokens * (cr_chars / total_chars))\n836\t        dollars = (\n837\t            round(cw_tokens * pricing[\"cache_write\"], 6) +\n838\t            round(cr_tokens * pricing[\"cache_read\"], 6)\n839\t        )\n840\t        return {\"tokens\": cw_tokens + cr_tokens, \"dollars\": dollars, \"chars\": cw_chars + cr_chars}\n841\t\n842\t    if total_chars > 0 and input_tokens > 0 and pricing:\n843\t        # Tool results (from user messages)\n844\t        tool_results = input_sources.get(\"tool_results\", {})\n845\t        if tool_results:\n846\t            tr_entry = {}\n847\t            for tool_name, char_dict in tool_results.items():\n848\t                tr_entry[tool_name] = _attribute_input_tool(char_dict)\n849\t            by_source[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"] = tr_entry\n850\t\n851\t        # Tool calls (from assistant messages)\n852\t        tool_calls_input = input_sources.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n853\t        if tool_calls_input:\n854\t            tc_entry = {}\n855\t            for tool_name, char_dict in tool_calls_input.items():\n856\t                tc_entry[tool_name] = _attribute_input_tool(char_dict)\n857\t            by_source[\"input\"][\"tool_calls\"] = tc_entry\n858\t\n859\t    # Output: distribute output tokens proportionally by character count\n860\t    output_cost_entry = cost_data.get(\"output\", {})\n861\t    output_tokens = output_cost_entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n862\t    output_dollars = output_cost_entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n863\t\n864\t    llm_chars = output_sources.get(\"llm_text\", 0)\n865\t    tc = output_sources.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n866\t    tc_total_chars = sum(tc.values())\n867\t    total_output_chars = llm_chars + tc_total_chars\n868\t\n869\t    if total_output_chars > 0 and output_tokens > 0:\n870\t        # LLM text\n871\t        llm_frac = llm_chars / total_output_chars\n872\t        by_source[\"output\"][\"llm_text\"] = {\n873\t            \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * llm_frac),\n874\t            \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * llm_frac, 6),\n875\t            \"chars\": llm_chars,\n876\t        }\n877\t\n878\t        # Tool calls\n879\t        tc_frac = tc_total_chars / total_output_chars\n880\t        tc_entry = {\n881\t            \"__total\": {\n882\t                \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * tc_frac),\n883\t                \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * tc_frac, 6),\n884\t                \"chars\": tc_total_chars,\n885\t            }\n886\t        }\n887\t        for tool_name, chars in tc.items():\n888\t            tool_frac = chars / total_output_chars\n889\t            tc_entry[tool_name] = {\n890\t                \"tokens\": round(output_tokens * tool_frac),\n891\t                \"dollars\": round(output_dollars * tool_frac, 6),\n892\t                \"chars\": chars,\n893\t            }\n894\t        by_source[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"] = tc_entry\n895\t\n896\t    return by_source\n897\t\n898\t\n899\tREAD_TOOLS = {\"read_file\", \"Read\", \"read_file_compressed\", \"read_file_uncompressed\"}\n900\tWRITE_TOOLS = {\"write_file\", \"Write\", \"edit_file\", \"Edit\"}\n901\t\n902\t\n903\t_PROJECT_ROOT = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\", \"..\"))\n904\t\n905\t\n906\tdef _get_file_path(input_data):\n907\t    \"\"\"Extract file path from tool input, checking common key names. Always returns an absolute path.\"\"\"\n908\t    if not isinstance(input_data, dict):\n909\t        return None\n910\t    fp = input_data.get(\"file_path\") or input_data.get(\"path\") or None\n911\t    if fp and not os.path.isabs(fp):\n912\t        fp = os.path.join(_PROJECT_ROOT, fp)\n913\t    return fp\n914\t\n915\t\n916\tdef extract_file_ops(body, response_path):\n917\t    \"\"\"Extract file operation stats from request body (reads) and response (writes).\n918\t\n919\t    Returns: {\n920\t        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": int, \"total_read_chars\": int, \"per_file\": {path: {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int}}},\n921\t        \"output\": {\"files_written\": int, \"total_write_chars\": int, \"per_file\": {path: {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int}}},\n922\t    }\n923\t    \"\"\"\n924\t    # --- Input: files read (from conversation history in request body) ---\n925\t    read_per_file = {}  # path -> {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int, \"tool_ids\": {id: chars}}\n926\t\n927\t    messages = body.get(\"messages\", [])\n928\t\n929\t    # Build tool_use_id -> (resolved_name, file_path) map from assistant messages\n930\t    tool_id_info = {}\n931\t    for msg in messages:\n932\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"assistant\":\n933\t            continue\n934\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n935\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n936\t            continue\n937\t        for block in content:\n938\t            if block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_use\":\n939\t                name = _resolve_read_file_name(block.get(\"name\", \"\"), block.get(\"input\", {}))\n940\t                if name in READ_TOOLS:\n941\t                    fp = _get_file_path(block.get(\"input\", {}))\n942\t                    tool_id_info[block.get(\"id\", \"\")] = fp\n943\t\n944\t    # Sum chars from tool_result blocks matching read tools\n945\t    for msg in messages:\n946\t        if msg.get(\"role\") != \"user\":\n947\t            continue\n948\t        content = msg.get(\"content\", [])\n949\t        if not isinstance(content, list):\n950\t            continue\n951\t        for block in content:\n952\t            if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_result\":\n953\t                continue\n954\t            tool_use_id = block.get(\"tool_use_id\", \"\")\n955\t            if tool_use_id not in tool_id_info:\n956\t                continue\n957\t            fp = tool_id_info[tool_use_id]\n958\t            result_content = block.get(\"content\", \"\")\n959\t            chars = 0\n960\t            if isinstance(result_content, str):\n961\t                chars = len(result_content)\n962\t            elif isinstance(result_content, list):\n963\t                chars = sum(len(b.get(\"text\", \"\")) for b in result_content)\n964\t            if fp:\n965\t                if fp not in read_per_file:\n966\t                    read_per_file[fp] = {\"calls\": 0, \"chars\": 0, \"tool_ids\": {}}\n967\t                read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"][tool_use_id] = chars\n968\t                read_per_file[fp][\"calls\"] = len(read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"])\n969\t                read_per_file[fp][\"chars\"] = sum(read_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"].values())\n970\t\n971\t    # --- Output: files written (from response) ---\n972\t    write_per_file = {}  # path -> {\"calls\": int, \"chars\": int, \"tool_ids\": {id: chars}}\n973\t\n974\t    response_blocks = parse_response_content(response_path)\n975\t    for block in response_blocks:\n976\t        if block.get(\"type\") != \"tool_use\":\n977\t            continue\n978\t        name = block.get(\"name\", \"\")\n979\t        if name not in WRITE_TOOLS:\n980\t            continue\n981\t        inp = block.get(\"input\", {})\n982\t        fp = _get_file_path(inp)\n983\t        # Sum content chars: \"content\" for Write/write_file, \"new_string\" for Edit/edit_file\n984\t        chars = 0\n985\t        if name in (\"Write\", \"write_file\"):\n986\t            chars = len(inp.get(\"content\", \"\"))\n987\t        elif name in (\"Edit\", \"edit_file\"):\n988\t            chars = len(inp.get(\"new_string\", \"\"))\n989\t        if fp:\n990\t            block_id = block.get(\"id\", \"\")\n991\t            if fp not in write_per_file:\n992\t                write_per_file[fp] = {\"calls\": 0, \"chars\": 0, \"tool_ids\": {}}\n993\t            write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"][block_id] = chars\n994\t            write_per_file[fp][\"calls\"] = len(write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"])\n995\t            write_per_file[fp][\"chars\"] = sum(write_per_file[fp][\"tool_ids\"].values())\n996\t\n997\t    # Add file_size for each file\n998\t    for pf in (read_per_file, write_per_file):\n999\t        for fp in pf:\n1000\t            try:\n1001\t                pf[fp][\"file_size\"] = os.path.getsize(fp)\n1002\t            except OSError:\n1003\t                pf[fp][\"file_size\"] = None\n1004\t\n1005\t    # Derive aggregate scalars from deduplicated per_file data\n1006\t    unique_files_read = len(read_per_file)\n1007\t    total_read_chars = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in read_per_file.values())\n1008\t    unique_files_written = len(write_per_file)\n1009\t    total_write_chars_dedup = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in write_per_file.values())\n1010\t    total_write_calls = sum(v[\"calls\"] for v in write_per_file.values())\n1011\t\n1012\t    return {\n1013\t        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": unique_files_read, \"total_read_chars\": total_read_chars, \"per_file\": read_per_file},\n1014\t        \"output\": {\"files_written\": total_write_calls, \"unique_files_written\": unique_files_written, \"total_write_chars\": total_write_chars_dedup, \"per_file\": write_per_file},\n1015\t    }\n1016\t\n1017\t\n1018\tdef extract_source_attribution(directory: str):\n1019\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, compute source attribution, read_file whitespace, and file ops.\"\"\"\n1020\t    count = 0\n1021\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n1022\t        if \"request.json\" not in filenames or \"usage.json\" not in filenames or \"response_raw.txt\" not in filenames:\n1023\t            continue\n1024\t\n1025\t        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n1026\t        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n1027\t        response_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"response_raw.txt\")\n1028\t\n1029\t        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n1030\t        if body is None:\n1031\t            continue\n1032\t\n1033\t        with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n1034\t            usage = json.load(f)\n1035\t\n1036\t        # Get model pricing\n1037\t        model = body.get(\"model\", \"\")\n1038\t        pricing = get_pricing(model) if model else None\n1039\t\n1040\t        # Compute source attribution\n1041\t        input_sources = categorize_input_sources(body)\n1042\t        output_sources = categorize_output_sources(response_path)\n1043\t        by_source = attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, pricing)\n1044\t\n1045\t        usage[\"by_source\"] = by_source\n1046\t\n1047\t        # Compute read_file whitespace\n1048\t        usage[\"read_file_whitespace\"] = extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n1049\t\n1050\t        # Compute file operations\n1051\t        usage[\"file_ops\"] = extract_file_ops(body, response_path)\n1052\t\n1053\t        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n1054\t            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n1055\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n1056\t        count += 1\n1057\t\n1058\t    print(f\"\\nExtracted source attribution for {count} flows\")\n1059\t\n1060\t\n1061\tdef calculate_costs(directory: str):\n1062\t    \"\"\"Walk output directory, compute dollar costs from usage.json and request.json model info.\"\"\"\n1063\t    count = 0\n1064\t    for dirpath, _dirnames, filenames in os.walk(directory):\n1065\t        if \"request.json\" not in filenames or \"usage.json\" not in filenames:\n1066\t            continue\n1067\t\n1068\t        request_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"request.json\")\n1069\t        body = parse_request_body(request_path)\n1070\t        if body is None:\n1071\t            continue\n1072\t\n1073\t        model = body.get(\"model\")\n1074\t        if not model:\n1075\t            continue\n1076\t\n1077\t        pricing = get_pricing(model)\n1078\t        if pricing is None:\n1079\t            print(f\"  Warning: unknown model '{model}' in {request_path}, skipping cost calculation\")\n1080\t            continue\n1081\t\n1082\t        usage_path = os.path.join(dirpath, \"usage.json\")\n1083\t        with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n1084\t            usage = json.load(f)\n1085\t\n1086\t        tokens_input = usage.get(\"input_tokens\", 0)\n1087\t        tokens_cache_write = usage.get(\"cache_creation_input_tokens\", 0)\n1088\t        tokens_cache_read = usage.get(\"cache_read_input_tokens\", 0)\n1089\t        tokens_output = usage.get(\"output_tokens\", 0)\n1090\t        tokens_total = tokens_input + tokens_cache_write + tokens_cache_read + tokens_output\n1091\t\n1092\t        cost_input = tokens_input * pricing[\"input\"]\n1093\t        cost_cache_write = tokens_cache_write * pricing[\"cache_write\"]\n1094\t        cost_cache_read = tokens_cache_read * pricing[\"cache_read\"]\n1095\t        cost_output = tokens_output * pricing[\"output\"]\n1096\t        cost_total = cost_input + cost_cache_write + cost_cache_read + cost_output\n1097\t\n1098\t        usage[\"cost\"] = {\n1099\t            \"input\": {\"tokens\": tokens_input, \"dollars\": round(cost_input, 6)},\n1100\t            \"cache_write\": {\"tokens\": tokens_cache_write, \"dollars\": round(cost_cache_write, 6)},\n1101\t            \"cache_read\": {\"tokens\": tokens_cache_read, \"dollars\": round(cost_cache_read, 6)},\n1102\t            \"output\": {\"tokens\": tokens_output, \"dollars\": round(cost_output, 6)},\n1103\t            \"total\": {\"tokens\": tokens_total, \"dollars\": round(cost_total, 6)},\n1104\t        }\n1105\t\n1106\t        # Remove top-level token keys (now redundant with cost entries)\n1107\t        for key in (\"input_tokens\", \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", \"cache_read_input_tokens\", \"output_tokens\"):\n1108\t            usage.pop(key, None)\n1109\t\n1110\t        canonical = get_canonical_model(model)\n1111\t        if canonical:\n1112\t            usage[\"model\"] = canonical\n1113\t\n1114\t        with open(usage_path, \"w\") as f:\n1115\t            json.dump(usage, f, indent=2)\n1116\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n1117\t        count += 1\n1118\t\n1119\t    print(f\"\\nCalculated costs for {count} flows\")\n1120\t\n1121\t\n1122\tdef _aggregate_by_source(agg, flow_by_source):\n1123\t    \"\"\"Aggregate per-flow by_source into summary by_source.\n1124\t\n1125\t    Input side: sum tool_results {tokens, dollars} dicts.\n1126\t    Output side: sum token/dollars dicts.\n1127\t    \"\"\"\n1128\t    # Input: tool_results and tool_calls are {tokens, dollars} dicts\n1129\t    flow_input = flow_by_source.get(\"input\", {})\n1130\t    for input_key in (\"tool_results\", \"tool_calls\"):\n1131\t        flow_section = flow_input.get(input_key, {})\n1132\t        if not flow_section:\n1133\t            continue\n1134\t        if input_key not in agg[\"input\"]:\n1135\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key] = {}\n1136\t        for tool, entry in flow_section.items():\n1137\t            if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n1138\t                continue\n1139\t            if tool not in agg[\"input\"][input_key]:\n1140\t                agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool] = {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 0}\n1141\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n1142\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n1143\t            agg[\"input\"][input_key][tool][\"chars\"] += entry.get(\"chars\", 0)\n1144\t\n1145\t    # Output: token/dollars dicts\n1146\t    flow_output = flow_by_source.get(\"output\", {})\n1147\t    for key in (\"llm_text\",):\n1148\t        entry = flow_output.get(key)\n1149\t        if entry:\n1150\t            if key not in agg[\"output\"]:\n1151\t                agg[\"output\"][key] = {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 0}\n1152\t            agg[\"output\"][key][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n1153\t            agg[\"output\"][key][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n1154\t            agg[\"output\"][key][\"chars\"] += entry.get(\"chars\", 0)\n1155\t\n1156\t    # Tool calls\n1157\t    flow_tc = flow_output.get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n1158\t    if flow_tc:\n1159\t        if \"tool_calls\" not in agg[\"output\"]:\n1160\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"] = {}\n1161\t        for tool_key, entry in flow_tc.items():\n1162\t            if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n1163\t                continue\n1164\t            if tool_key not in agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"]:\n1165\t                agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key] = {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 0}\n1166\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n1167\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n1168\t            agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][tool_key][\"chars\"] += entry.get(\"chars\", 0)\n1169\t\n1170\t\n1171\tdef _round_by_source(agg):\n1172\t    \"\"\"Round dollar values in the by_source aggregate.\"\"\"\n1173\t    # Input: round dollars\n1174\t    for input_key in (\"tool_results\", \"tool_calls\"):\n1175\t        section = agg.get(\"input\", {}).get(input_key, {})\n1176\t        for entry in section.values():\n1177\t            if isinstance(entry, dict) and \"dollars\" in entry:\n1178\t                entry[\"dollars\"] = round(entry[\"dollars\"], 6)\n1179\t    # Output: round dollars\n1180\t    for key in (\"llm_text\",):\n1181\t        entry = agg.get(\"output\", {}).get(key)\n1182\t        if entry:\n1183\t            entry[\"dollars\"] = round(entry[\"dollars\"], 6)\n1184\t    tc = agg.get(\"output\", {}).get(\"tool_calls\", {})\n1185\t    for entry in tc.values():\n1186\t        if isinstance(entry, dict) and \"dollars\" in entry:\n1187\t            entry[\"dollars\"] = round(entry[\"dollars\"], 6)\n1188\t\n1189\t\n1190\tAGENT_COLORS = {\n1191\t    \"vix\": \"#7B2FBE\",\n1192\t    \"cc\": \"#D77656\",\n1193\t}\n1194\t\n1195\t\n1196\tdef _agent_color(name):\n1197\t    \"\"\"Return a deterministic hex color for an unknown agent name.\"\"\"\n1198\t    import hashlib\n1199\t    h = int(hashlib.md5(name.encode()).hexdigest()[:6], 16)\n1200\t    return f\"#{h:06x}\"\n1201\t\n1202\t\n1203\tdef summarize_usage(directory: str):\n1204\t    \"\"\"Aggregate per-request usage.json files into a summary usage.json per agent type.\"\"\"\n1205\t    COST_FIELDS = [\"input\", \"cache_write\", \"cache_read\", \"output\", \"total\"]\n1206\t\n1207\t    def empty_bucket():\n1208\t        bucket = {\"request_count\": 0}\n1209\t        bucket[\"cost\"] = {f: {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0} for f in COST_FIELDS}\n1210\t        bucket[\"timing\"] = {\n1211\t            \"total_duration_ms\": 0,\n1212\t            \"min_request_start\": None, \"max_response_end\": None,\n1213\t        }\n1214\t        return bucket\n1215\t\n1216\t    def add_to_bucket(bucket, usage):\n1217\t        bucket[\"request_count\"] += 1\n1218\t        cost = usage.get(\"cost\")\n1219\t        if cost:\n1220\t            for f in COST_FIELDS:\n1221\t                entry = cost.get(f, {})\n1222\t                if isinstance(entry, dict):\n1223\t                    bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"tokens\"] += entry.get(\"tokens\", 0)\n1224\t                    bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"dollars\"] += entry.get(\"dollars\", 0.0)\n1225\t        timing = usage.get(\"timing\")\n1226\t        if timing:\n1227\t            bucket[\"timing\"][\"total_duration_ms\"] += timing.get(\"duration_ms\", 0)\n1228\t            rs = timing.get(\"request_start\")\n1229\t            re_ = timing.get(\"response_end\")\n1230\t            if rs is not None:\n1231\t                cur = bucket[\"timing\"][\"min_request_start\"]\n1232\t                bucket[\"timing\"][\"min_request_start\"] = rs if cur is None else min(cur, rs)\n1233\t            if re_ is not None:\n1234\t                cur = bucket[\"timing\"][\"max_response_end\"]\n1235\t                bucket[\"timing\"][\"max_response_end\"] = re_ if cur is None else max(cur, re_)\n1236\t\n1237\t    def round_costs(bucket):\n1238\t        for f in COST_FIELDS:\n1239\t            bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"dollars\"] = round(bucket[\"cost\"][f][\"dollars\"], 6)\n1240\t\n1241\t    count = 0\n1242\t    for entry in sorted(os.listdir(directory)):\n1243\t        agent_dir = os.path.join(directory, entry)\n1244\t        if not os.path.isdir(agent_dir):\n1245\t            continue\n1246\t\n1247\t        # Only process dirs that contain numbered step subdirs\n1248\t        has_numbered = False\n1249\t        for sub in os.listdir(agent_dir):\n1250\t            if sub.isdigit() and os.path.isdir(os.path.join(agent_dir, sub)):\n1251\t                has_numbered = True\n1252\t                break\n1253\t        if not has_numbered:\n1254\t            continue\n1255\t\n1256\t        by_model = {}\n1257\t        by_step = {}\n1258\t        total = empty_bucket()\n1259\t        ws_agg = {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n1260\t        by_source_agg = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n1261\t        file_ops_agg = {\n1262\t            \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": 0, \"total_read_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n1263\t            \"output\": {\"files_written\": 0, \"unique_files_written\": 0, \"total_write_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n1264\t        }\n1265\t\n1266\t        # Iterate step dirs: {agent_dir}/{step_number}/\n1267\t        for step_sub in sorted(os.listdir(agent_dir), key=lambda x: int(x) if x.isdigit() else float(\"inf\")):\n1268\t            if not step_sub.isdigit():\n1269\t                continue\n1270\t            step_dir = os.path.join(agent_dir, step_sub)\n1271\t            if not os.path.isdir(step_dir):\n1272\t                continue\n1273\t\n1274\t            step_key = step_sub  # Use step directory number as key\n1275\t\n1276\t            # Iterate request dirs: {step_dir}/{request_number}/usage.json\n1277\t            for req_sub in sorted(os.listdir(step_dir), key=lambda x: int(x) if x.isdigit() else float(\"inf\")):\n1278\t                if not req_sub.isdigit():\n1279\t                    continue\n1280\t                usage_path = os.path.join(step_dir, req_sub, \"usage.json\")\n1281\t                if not os.path.isfile(usage_path):\n1282\t                    continue\n1283\t\n1284\t                with open(usage_path, \"r\") as f:\n1285\t                    usage = json.load(f)\n1286\t\n1287\t                model_name = usage.get(\"model\", \"unknown\")\n1288\t                if model_name not in by_model:\n1289\t                    by_model[model_name] = empty_bucket()\n1290\t                add_to_bucket(by_model[model_name], usage)\n1291\t\n1292\t                add_to_bucket(total, usage)\n1293\t\n1294\t                # Aggregate by_source\n1295\t                flow_by_source = usage.get(\"by_source\")\n1296\t                if flow_by_source:\n1297\t                    _aggregate_by_source(by_source_agg, flow_by_source)\n1298\t\n1299\t                # Aggregate read_file whitespace\n1300\t                flow_ws = usage.get(\"read_file_whitespace\")\n1301\t                if flow_ws:\n1302\t                    for k in (\"line_returns_count\", \"unnecessary_space_count\", \"total_chars\"):\n1303\t                        ws_agg[k] += flow_ws.get(k, 0)\n1304\t\n1305\t                # Aggregate file_ops\n1306\t                flow_file_ops = usage.get(\"file_ops\")\n1307\t                if flow_file_ops:\n1308\t                    fi = flow_file_ops.get(\"input\", {})\n1309\t                    fo = flow_file_ops.get(\"output\", {})\n1310\t                    # Scalar fields will be recomputed from deduplicated per_file after aggregation\n1311\t                    # Aggregate per-file details (merge tool_ids maps for dedup)\n1312\t                    for side in (\"input\", \"output\"):\n1313\t                        for fp, stats in fi.get(\"per_file\", {}).items() if side == \"input\" else fo.get(\"per_file\", {}).items():\n1314\t                            agg_pf = file_ops_agg[side][\"per_file\"]\n1315\t                            if fp not in agg_pf:\n1316\t                                agg_pf[fp] = {\"tool_ids\": {}, \"file_size\": stats.get(\"file_size\")}\n1317\t                            for tid, tc in stats.get(\"tool_ids\", {}).items():\n1318\t                                agg_pf[fp][\"tool_ids\"][tid] = tc\n1319\t\n1320\t                # Aggregate per step\n1321\t                if step_key not in by_step:\n1322\t                    by_step[step_key] = empty_bucket()\n1323\t                    by_step[step_key][\"by_source\"] = {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n1324\t                    by_step[step_key][\"read_file_whitespace\"] = {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n1325\t                    by_step[step_key][\"file_ops\"] = {\n1326\t                        \"input\": {\"unique_files_read\": 0, \"total_read_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n1327\t                        \"output\": {\"files_written\": 0, \"unique_files_written\": 0, \"total_write_chars\": 0, \"per_file\": {}},\n1328\t                    }\n1329\t                add_to_bucket(by_step[step_key], usage)\n1330\t                if flow_by_source:\n1331\t                    _aggregate_by_source(by_step[step_key][\"by_source\"], flow_by_source)\n1332\t                if flow_ws:\n1333\t                    for k in (\"line_returns_count\", \"unnecessary_space_count\", \"total_chars\"):\n1334\t                        by_step[step_key][\"read_file_whitespace\"][k] += flow_ws.get(k, 0)\n1335\t                if flow_file_ops:\n1336\t                    fi = flow_file_ops.get(\"input\", {})\n1337\t                    fo = flow_file_ops.get(\"output\", {})\n1338\t                    # Scalar fields will be recomputed from deduplicated per_file after aggregation\n1339\t                    for side in (\"input\", \"output\"):\n1340\t                        for fp, stats in fi.get(\"per_file\", {}).items() if side == \"input\" else fo.get(\"per_file\", {}).items():\n1341\t                            agg_pf = by_step[step_key][\"file_ops\"][side][\"per_file\"]\n1342\t                            if fp not in agg_pf:\n1343\t                                agg_pf[fp] = {\"tool_ids\": {}, \"file_size\": stats.get(\"file_size\")}\n1344\t                            for tid, tc in stats.get(\"tool_ids\", {}).items():\n1345\t                                agg_pf[fp][\"tool_ids\"][tid] = tc\n1346\t\n1347\t        round_costs(total)\n1348\t        for bucket in by_model.values():\n1349\t            round_costs(bucket)\n1350\t        for bucket in by_step.values():\n1351\t            round_costs(bucket)\n1352\t            if \"by_source\" in bucket:\n1353\t                _round_by_source(bucket[\"by_source\"])\n1354\t        _round_by_source(by_source_agg)\n1355\t\n1356\t        # Finalize file_ops: convert tool_ids maps to calls/chars, recompute scalars\n1357\t        def _finalize_file_ops(fops):\n1358\t            for side in (\"input\", \"output\"):\n1359\t                pf = fops[side][\"per_file\"]\n1360\t                for fp in pf:\n1361\t                    pf[fp][\"calls\"] = len(pf[fp].get(\"tool_ids\", {}))\n1362\t                    pf[fp][\"chars\"] = sum(pf[fp].get(\"tool_ids\", {}).values())\n1363\t                    pf[fp].pop(\"tool_ids\", None)\n1364\t            fops[\"input\"][\"unique_files_read\"] = len(fops[\"input\"][\"per_file\"])\n1365\t            fops[\"input\"][\"total_read_chars\"] = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in fops[\"input\"][\"per_file\"].values())\n1366\t            fops[\"output\"][\"unique_files_written\"] = len(fops[\"output\"][\"per_file\"])\n1367\t            fops[\"output\"][\"files_written\"] = sum(v[\"calls\"] for v in fops[\"output\"][\"per_file\"].values())\n1368\t            fops[\"output\"][\"total_write_chars\"] = sum(v[\"chars\"] for v in fops[\"output\"][\"per_file\"].values())\n1369\t\n1370\t        _finalize_file_ops(file_ops_agg)\n1371\t        for bucket in by_step.values():\n1372\t            if \"file_ops\" in bucket:\n1373\t                _finalize_file_ops(bucket[\"file_ops\"])\n1374\t\n1375\t        # Finalize timing for each bucket\n1376\t        def _finalize_timing(bucket):\n1377\t            t = bucket[\"timing\"]\n1378\t            req_count = bucket[\"request_count\"]\n1379\t            mn = t.pop(\"min_request_start\", None)\n1380\t            mx = t.pop(\"max_response_end\", None)\n1381\t            if mn is not None and mx is not None:\n1382\t                t[\"wall_clock_ms\"] = round((mx - mn) * 1000)\n1383\t            else:\n1384\t                t[\"wall_clock_ms\"] = 0\n1385\t            t[\"avg_duration_ms\"] = round(t[\"total_duration_ms\"] / req_count) if req_count > 0 else 0\n1386\t\n1387\t        _finalize_timing(total)\n1388\t        for bucket in by_model.values():\n1389\t            _finalize_timing(bucket)\n1390\t        for bucket in by_step.values():\n1391\t            _finalize_timing(bucket)\n1392\t\n1393\t        total[\"file_ops\"] = file_ops_agg\n1394\t        summary = {\"title\": entry, \"color\": AGENT_COLORS.get(entry, _agent_color(entry)), \"by_model\": by_model, \"by_step\": by_step, \"by_source\": by_source_agg, \"read_file_whitespace\": ws_agg, \"total\": total}\n1395\t        summary_path = os.path.join(agent_dir, \"usage.json\")\n1396\t        with open(summary_path, \"w\") as f:\n1397\t            json.dump(summary, f, indent=2)\n1398\t            f.write(\"\\n\")\n1399\t        count += 1\n1400\t        print(f\"  Wrote summary: {summary_path} ({total['request_count']} requests)\")\n1401\t\n1402\t    print(f\"\\nSummarized usage for {count} agent types\")\n1403\t\n1404\t\n1405\tdef main():\n1406\t    script_dir = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\n1407\t    data_dir = os.path.join(script_dir, \"data\")\n1408\t\n1409\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Export mitmproxy flow files to text.\")\n1410\t    parser.add_argument(\"--input-directory\", default=data_dir, help=\"Directory containing *.flow files (default: data/ next to script)\")\n1411\t    parser.add_argument(\"--output-directory\", default=data_dir, help=\"Output directory for exported flows (default: data/ next to script)\")\n1412\t    args = parser.parse_args()\n1413\t\n1414\t    input_dir = args.input_directory\n1415\t    output_dir = args.output_directory\n1416\t    os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n1417\t\n1418\t    redact_flow_files(input_dir)\n1419\t    export_flows(input_dir, output_dir)\n1420\t    extract_usage(output_dir)\n1421\t    export_parsed_responses(output_dir)\n1422\t    extract_prompts(output_dir)\n1423\t    calculate_costs(output_dir)\n1424\t    extract_source_attribution(output_dir)\n1425\t    summarize_usage(output_dir)\n1426\t\n1427\t\n1428\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n1429\t    main()\n1430\t"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KYRbSZzPQpmPXyPqbpL9rw","name":"Glob","input":{"pattern":"**/conftest.py"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PnHeZThjXk4cSxmUKyyESx","name":"Glob","input":{"pattern":"**/pytest.ini"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fa7peUKp6X1jSX4dNau1mM","name":"Glob","input":{"pattern":"**/setup.cfg"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KYRbSZzPQpmPXyPqbpL9rw","type":"tool_result","content":"No files found"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PnHeZThjXk4cSxmUKyyESx","type":"tool_result","content":"No files found"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fa7peUKp6X1jSX4dNau1mM","type":"tool_result","content":"No files found"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y5BtWbHbM7DhrDDw2z5Yd1","name":"Glob","input":{"pattern":"**/*.toml"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016wpDLspnePi8HT9ZCv4FtV","name":"Glob","input":{"pattern":"**/requirements*.txt"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y5BtWbHbM7DhrDDw2z5Yd1","type":"tool_result","content":"No files found"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016wpDLspnePi8HT9ZCv4FtV","type":"tool_result","content":"No files found\n\n<system-reminder>\nThe task tools haven't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using TaskCreate to add new tasks and TaskUpdate to update task status (set to in_progress when starting, completed when done). Also consider cleaning up the task list if it has become stale. Only use these if relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable. Make sure that you NEVER mention this reminder to the user\n\n</system-reminder>"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I have everything I need. Let me write the plan."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YL1ihBcZdA1HaScz9HYLeG","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/.claude/plans/zippy-purring-island.md","content":"# Plan: Write Tests for export_flows.py\n\n## Context\nThe file `/workspace/export_flows.py` (1430 lines) exports mitmproxy flow files into structured per-flow directories and performs token usage analysis. The user wants a comprehensive pytest suite at `/workspace/evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py` achieving ‚â•80% code coverage. No existing tests, no pytest config. mitmproxy is an external dependency requiring mocking.\n\n## Target file\n`/workspace/export_flows.py` ‚Äî imported as `export_flows` with `sys.path` insertion in test file.\n\n## Test file to create\n`/workspace/evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py`\n\nThe test file will use:\n- `pytest` + `unittest.mock` (patch, MagicMock)\n- `pytest`'s `tmp_path` fixture for real filesystem operations\n- Manual mock objects for mitmproxy types (HTTPFlow, headers)\n\n---\n\n## Test Suite Structure\n\n### 1. Pure-logic utility functions (no I/O)\n\n**`count_whitespace_stats`**\n- Empty string ‚Üí all zeros\n- String with newlines ‚Üí correct count\n- String with multi-space runs ‚Üí correct unnecessary count (len-1 per run)\n- Mixed content\n\n**`get_canonical_model`**\n- Exact match: `\"claude-sonnet-4-6\"` ‚Üí `\"claude-sonnet-4-6\"`\n- Date-suffix: `\"claude-opus-4-5-20241022\"` ‚Üí `\"claude-opus-4-5\"` (not `\"claude-opus-4\"`)\n- Longer prefix wins: `\"claude-opus-4-5-x\"` ‚Üí `\"claude-opus-4-5\"` (sorted longest-first)\n- Unknown model ‚Üí None\n- Empty string ‚Üí None\n\n**`get_pricing`**\n- Known model with suffix ‚Üí returns pricing dict\n- Unknown model ‚Üí None\n\n**`sanitize_path`**\n- Query string stripped: `\"/v1/messages?foo=bar\"` ‚Üí no `?foo=bar`\n- Slashes replaced with `_`, leading/trailing stripped\n- Special chars removed\n- Result truncated at 80 chars\n\n**`_resolve_read_file_name`**\n- `\"read_file\"` + `{\"mode\": \"compress\"}` ‚Üí `\"read_file_compressed\"`\n- `\"read_file\"` + `{\"mode\": \"original\"}` ‚Üí `\"read_file_uncompressed\"`\n- `\"read_file\"` + `{}` ‚Üí `\"read_file_uncompressed\"` (default)\n- `\"read_file\"` + non-dict input ‚Üí `\"read_file_uncompressed\"`\n- Other tool name ‚Üí returned unchanged\n\n**`_format_tool_params`**\n- String value ‚Üí quoted: `key=\"value\"`\n- Non-string value ‚Üí json.dumps: `key=123`\n- Mixed types\n- Empty dict ‚Üí empty string\n\n**`_agent_color`**\n- Known agents use AGENT_COLORS lookup (vix, cc)\n- Unknown agent: deterministic hex via MD5\n- Same name called twice ‚Üí same color\n\n**`_system_prompt_hash`**\n- Body with system array at correct index ‚Üí 12-char hex\n- Body missing system key ‚Üí None\n- Index out of range ‚Üí None\n- Empty text at index ‚Üí None\n- `\"cc\"` uses index 2, `\"vix\"` uses index 0\n\n**`_get_file_path`**\n- `{\"file_path\": \"/abs/path\"}` ‚Üí `/abs/path`\n- `{\"path\": \"/abs/path\"}` ‚Üí `/abs/path`\n- Relative path ‚Üí joined with `_PROJECT_ROOT`\n- Non-dict ‚Üí None\n- Neither key ‚Üí None\n\n**`_aggregate_by_source`**\n- Tool results accumulated correctly across multiple flows\n- Tool calls accumulated correctly\n- LLM text accumulated\n- Missing keys handled gracefully\n\n**`_round_by_source`**\n- Dollar values rounded to 6 decimal places\n- Input tool_results, tool_calls, output llm_text, tool_calls all rounded\n\n### 2. File-reading functions (mock `open` or use `tmp_path`)\n\n**`parse_request_body`**\n- Valid JSON file ‚Üí dict returned\n- Invalid JSON ‚Üí None\n- Use `tmp_path` for real file writes\n\n**`format_headers`**\n- Regular header ‚Üí `\"key: value\"`\n- `x-api-key` ‚Üí `\"x-api-key: [REDACTED]\"`\n- `authorization` ‚Üí `\"authorization: [REDACTED]\"`\n- Uses mock object with `.fields` attribute returning list of `(bytes, bytes)` tuples\n\n**`extract_stop_reason`** (takes string, no file I/O)\n- SSE with `message_delta` containing stop_reason\n- SSE with compact JSON (`\"type\":\"message_delta\"`)\n- SSE with spaced JSON (`\"type\": \"message_delta\"`)\n- Non-streaming JSON with `type==message`\n- No matching content ‚Üí `\"unknown\"`\n- Malformed JSON lines skipped\n\n### 3. File I/O functions (use `tmp_path`)\n\n**`write_request`** (mock HTTPFlow)\n- Creates `request_headers.txt` with method + URL + formatted headers\n- Creates `request.json` with pretty-printed JSON body\n- Creates `request.json` with raw body when JSON parse fails\n- No body ‚Üí no request.json file\n\n**`write_response`** (mock HTTPFlow)\n- `flow.response is None` ‚Üí returns early, no file created\n- Valid response ‚Üí writes `response_raw.txt` with status + headers + body\n- Response with no body text ‚Üí no blank-line+body section\n\n**`extract_usage`** (use `tmp_path`)\n- SSE format: extracts from `message_delta` event\n- Non-streaming fallback: extracts from JSON `type==message`\n- Merges `timing.json` when present and removes it\n- Computes `duration_ms` when both timestamps present\n- No usage found ‚Üí warning printed, no `usage.json`\n- Filters to only TOKEN_FIELDS\n\n**`extract_prompts`** (use `tmp_path`)\n- Extracts system text blocks and joins with `\\n\\n`\n- Finds first user message, concatenates text blocks\n- Skips non-text blocks\n- Empty system ‚Üí no `system_prompt.md`\n- No user message ‚Üí no `first_user_message.md`\n- Invalid JSON body ‚Üí warning, skip\n\n**`extract_read_file_whitespace`** (pure logic, dict input)\n- Tool use in assistant ‚Üí tool result in user mapped correctly\n- `read_file` with compress mode ‚Üí `read_file_compressed` matches\n- `Read` tool name ‚Üí matches\n- Non-read tool ‚Üí excluded\n- String content in tool result\n- List content in tool result (concatenated)\n- Missing tool_use_id ‚Üí \"unknown\" tool name, doesn't match read filter\n\n**`categorize_input_sources`** (pure logic, dict input)\n- Last user message content ‚Üí cache_write\n- Earlier user message content ‚Üí cache_read\n- Second-to-last assistant message tool_use ‚Üí cache_write\n- Other assistant messages ‚Üí cache_read\n- total_chars is length of `json.dumps(body)`\n- Empty messages ‚Üí empty tool_results/tool_calls\n\n**`categorize_output_sources`** (use `tmp_path`)\n- SSE: full content_block_start‚Üídelta‚Üístop sequence for text block\n- SSE: tool_use block with input_json_delta ‚Üí resolves read_file name\n- Multiple blocks at different indices\n- Invalid JSON delta ‚Üí input_data = {}\n- Non-streaming fallback for text + tool_use blocks\n- Empty file ‚Üí zeros\n\n**`parse_response_content`** (use `tmp_path`)\n- SSE: text block assembled from deltas\n- SSE: tool_use block with JSON assembled\n- Non-streaming: extracts text and tool_use\n- Returns empty list for no content\n\n**`export_parsed_response`** (use `tmp_path`)\n- Text block written as-is\n- Tool_use block written as `[ToolName(params)]`\n- Empty blocks ‚Üí returns False, no file written\n- Returns True on success\n\n**`attribute_tokens`** (pure logic)\n- Proportional distribution of output tokens\n- Input tokens attributed by cache_write/cache_read chars\n- `total_chars == 0` ‚Üí input section skipped\n- `total_output_chars == 0` ‚Üí output section skipped\n- Multiple tools in output ‚Üí each gets proportional share\n- `__total` key added to output tool_calls\n\n**`extract_file_ops`** (use `tmp_path` for response file)\n- Read tools: sums chars from tool_result content (string)\n- Read tools: sums chars from tool_result content (list of blocks)\n- Write tool (`Write`): counts `content` chars\n- Edit tool (`Edit`): counts `new_string` chars\n- Absolute file_path used directly, relative joined with _PROJECT_ROOT\n- File size: OSError ‚Üí None\n- Deduplication via tool_ids map\n\n**`calculate_costs`** (use `tmp_path`)\n- Known model: computes correct dollar amounts\n- Unknown model ‚Üí warning, skip\n- Missing model field ‚Üí skip\n- Removes top-level token keys\n- Adds canonical model name to usage\n\n### 4. mitmproxy-dependent functions (mock FlowReader/FlowWriter)\n\n**`redact_flow_files`**\n- No `.flow` files ‚Üí returns immediately\n- HTTP flow with `x-api-key` ‚Üí redacted + file rewritten\n- No sensitive headers ‚Üí not rewritten\n- `FlowReadException` ‚Üí skip with message\n- Non-HTTPFlow object ‚Üí appended but not modified\n\n**`export_flows`**\n- No `.flow` files ‚Üí prints message and returns\n- Skips flows with `/count_token` in URL\n- Skips \"quota\" requests\n- `cc` agent: step increments on system prompt hash change\n- Non-`cc` agent: step increments on `end_turn` stop_reason\n- `FlowReadException` ‚Üí skip with message\n- Correct directory structure: `{agent}/{step}/{request}/`\n- `timing.json` written for each flow\n\n### 5. Aggregation / summary function (use `tmp_path`)\n\n**`summarize_usage`**\n- Skips non-directory entries\n- Skips agent dirs with no numbered subdirs\n- Aggregates cost across requests and models\n- `by_step` grouped by step subdirectory number\n- Timing: `wall_clock_ms` = (max_response_end - min_request_start) * 1000\n- `avg_duration_ms` computed\n- `file_ops` finalized: tool_ids removed, scalars recomputed\n- Known agent color (vix, cc) vs unknown agent (MD5 hash)\n- Writes `usage.json` to agent dir\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n### Mock for mitmproxy HTTPFlow\n```python\ndef make_mock_flow(method=\"POST\", url=\"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages\",\n                   body='{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-6\"}',\n                   status=200, reason=\"OK\", response_body=\"\",\n                   req_ts=1000.0, resp_ts=2000.0):\n    flow = MagicMock()\n    flow.request.method = method\n    flow.request.pretty_url = url\n    flow.request.headers.fields = []\n    flow.request.get_text.return_value = body\n    flow.request.timestamp_start = req_ts\n    flow.response.status_code = status\n    flow.response.reason = reason\n    flow.response.headers.fields = []\n    flow.response.get_text.return_value = response_body\n    flow.response.timestamp_end = resp_ts\n    return flow\n```\n\n### Import handling\nThe test file will use:\n```python\nimport sys, os\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\", \"..\"))\nimport export_flows\nfrom export_flows import ...\n```\n\n### SSE response fixture\n```python\nSSE_RESPONSE = \"\"\"200 OK\n\ncontent-type: text/event-stream\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"content_block_start\",\"index\":0,\"content_block\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"name\":\"\"}}\ndata: {\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"Hello\"}}\ndata: {\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":0}\ndata: {\"type\":\"message_delta\",\"delta\":{\"stop_reason\":\"end