ection skipped\n- Multiple tools in output ‚Üí each gets proportional share\n- `__total` key added to output tool_calls\n\n**`extract_file_ops`** (use `tmp_path` for response file)\n- Read tools: sums chars from tool_result content (string)\n- Read tools: sums chars from tool_result content (list of blocks)\n- Write tool (`Write`): counts `content` chars\n- Edit tool (`Edit`): counts `new_string` chars\n- Absolute file_path used directly, relative joined with _PROJECT_ROOT\n- File size: OSError ‚Üí None\n- Deduplication via tool_ids map\n\n**`calculate_costs`** (use `tmp_path`)\n- Known model: computes correct dollar amounts\n- Unknown model ‚Üí warning, skip\n- Missing model field ‚Üí skip\n- Removes top-level token keys\n- Adds canonical model name to usage\n\n### 4. mitmproxy-dependent functions (mock FlowReader/FlowWriter)\n\n**`redact_flow_files`**\n- No `.flow` files ‚Üí returns immediately\n- HTTP flow with `x-api-key` ‚Üí redacted + file rewritten\n- No sensitive headers ‚Üí not rewritten\n- `FlowReadException` ‚Üí skip with message\n- Non-HTTPFlow object ‚Üí appended but not modified\n\n**`export_flows`**\n- No `.flow` files ‚Üí prints message and returns\n- Skips flows with `/count_token` in URL\n- Skips \"quota\" requests\n- `cc` agent: step increments on system prompt hash change\n- Non-`cc` agent: step increments on `end_turn` stop_reason\n- `FlowReadException` ‚Üí skip with message\n- Correct directory structure: `{agent}/{step}/{request}/`\n- `timing.json` written for each flow\n\n### 5. Aggregation / summary function (use `tmp_path`)\n\n**`summarize_usage`**\n- Skips non-directory entries\n- Skips agent dirs with no numbered subdirs\n- Aggregates cost across requests and models\n- `by_step` grouped by step subdirectory number\n- Timing: `wall_clock_ms` = (max_response_end - min_request_start) * 1000\n- `avg_duration_ms` computed\n- `file_ops` finalized: tool_ids removed, scalars recomputed\n- Known agent color (vix, cc) vs unknown agent (MD5 hash)\n- Writes `usage.json` to agent dir\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n### Mock for mitmproxy HTTPFlow\n```python\ndef make_mock_flow(method=\"POST\", url=\"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages\",\n                   body='{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-6\"}',\n                   status=200, reason=\"OK\", response_body=\"\",\n                   req_ts=1000.0, resp_ts=2000.0):\n    flow = MagicMock()\n    flow.request.method = method\n    flow.request.pretty_url = url\n    flow.request.headers.fields = []\n    flow.request.get_text.return_value = body\n    flow.request.timestamp_start = req_ts\n    flow.response.status_code = status\n    flow.response.reason = reason\n    flow.response.headers.fields = []\n    flow.response.get_text.return_value = response_body\n    flow.response.timestamp_end = resp_ts\n    return flow\n```\n\n### Import handling\nThe test file will use:\n```python\nimport sys, os\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\", \"..\"))\nimport export_flows\nfrom export_flows import ...\n```\n\n### SSE response fixture\n```python\nSSE_RESPONSE = \"\"\"200 OK\n\ncontent-type: text/event-stream\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"content_block_start\",\"index\":0,\"content_block\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"name\":\"\"}}\ndata: {\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"Hello\"}}\ndata: {\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":0}\ndata: {\"type\":\"message_delta\",\"delta\":{\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\"},\"usage\":{\"output_tokens\":5}}\n\"\"\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Verification\n\nRun with coverage:\n```bash\ncd /workspace && python -m pytest evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py -v \\\n  --cov=export_flows --cov-report=term-missing\n```\n\nTarget: ‚â•80% line coverage. The main uncovered areas are likely:\n- `main()` function (argparse + orchestration) ‚Äî acceptable to skip\n- Some error branches in `summarize_usage` deep nesting\n\n<system-reminder>\n## Exited Plan Mode\n\nYou have exited plan mode. You can now make edits, run tools, and take actions. The plan file is located at /root/.claude/plans/zippy-purring-island.md if you need to reference it.\n</system-reminder>","tool_use_id":"toolu_01X8WhG4YkPvuBswMVzWKFfz"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CmQ9wyV6DjPaiFsmvg2puU","name":"TaskCreate","input":{"subject":"Write comprehensive test suite for export_flows.py","description":"Create /workspace/evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py with pytest tests covering ‚â•80% of export_flows.py. Use mocks for mitmproxy and filesystem as needed.","activeForm":"Writing test suite"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CmQ9wyV6DjPaiFsmvg2puU","type":"tool_result","content":"Task #1 created successfully: Write comprehensive test suite for export_flows.py"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MqA6zKF4M2SoQZKtar4uBu","name":"TaskUpdate","input":{"taskId":"1","status":"in_progress"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MqA6zKF4M2SoQZKtar4uBu","type":"tool_result","content":"Updated task #1 status"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fb6WovHP74chcWaxLD4sEQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p /workspace/evaluation/usage","description":"Create evaluation/usage directory"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fb6WovHP74chcWaxLD4sEQ","type":"tool_result","content":"(Bash completed with no output)","is_error":false}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013cUbN94nuTdnaEAbvTdNxs","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py","content":"\"\"\"Comprehensive tests for export_flows.py targeting ‚â•80% code coverage.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\n\nimport pytest\nfrom unittest.mock import MagicMock, patch, mock_open, call\n\n# Allow importing export_flows from the workspace root\nsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\", \"..\"))\n\nimport export_flows\nfrom export_flows import (\n    count_whitespace_stats,\n    get_canonical_model,\n    get_pricing,\n    sanitize_path,\n    _resolve_read_file_name,\n    _format_tool_params,\n    _agent_color,\n    _system_prompt_hash,\n    _get_file_path,\n    _aggregate_by_source,\n    _round_by_source,\n    parse_request_body,\n    format_headers,\n    extract_stop_reason,\n    write_request,\n    write_response,\n    extract_usage,\n    extract_prompts,\n    extract_read_file_whitespace,\n    categorize_input_sources,\n    categorize_output_sources,\n    parse_response_content,\n    export_parsed_response,\n    attribute_tokens,\n    extract_file_ops,\n    calculate_costs,\n    redact_flow_files,\n    export_flows as _export_flows,\n    summarize_usage,\n    AGENT_COLORS,\n    MODEL_PRICING,\n)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Helpers / fixtures\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef make_headers_mock(fields):\n    \"\"\"Return a mock headers object with .fields = [(bytes, bytes), ...].\"\"\"\n    h = MagicMock()\n    h.fields = fields\n    return h\n\n\ndef make_mock_flow(\n    method=\"POST\",\n    url=\"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages\",\n    body='{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\"messages\":[]}',\n    req_headers=None,\n    status=200,\n    reason=\"OK\",\n    response_body=\"\",\n    resp_headers=None,\n    req_ts=1000.0,\n    resp_ts=2000.0,\n    no_response=False,\n):\n    flow = MagicMock()\n    flow.request.method = method\n    flow.request.pretty_url = url\n    flow.request.headers = make_headers_mock(req_headers or [])\n    flow.request.get_text.return_value = body\n    flow.request.timestamp_start = req_ts\n\n    if no_response:\n        flow.response = None\n    else:\n        flow.response.status_code = status\n        flow.response.reason = reason\n        flow.response.headers = make_headers_mock(resp_headers or [])\n        flow.response.get_text.return_value = response_body\n        flow.response.timestamp_end = resp_ts\n    return flow\n\n\nSSE_RESPONSE_WITH_USAGE = (\n    \"200 OK\\n\\ncontent-type: text/event-stream\\n\\n\"\n    'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_start\",\"index\":0,\"content_block\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"name\":\"\"}}\\n'\n    'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"text_delta\",\"text\":\"Hello world\"}}\\n'\n    'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":0}\\n'\n    'data: {\"type\":\"message_delta\",\"delta\":{\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\"},'\n    '\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":10,\"output_tokens\":5,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":3}}\\n'\n)\n\nNONSTREAM_RESPONSE = (\n    \"200 OK\\n\\ncontent-type: application/json\\n\\n\"\n    '{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"msg_1\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Hi\"}],'\n    '\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":8,\"output_tokens\":3},\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\"}'\n)\n\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# 1. Pure-logic utility functions\n# ===========================================================================\n\n\nclass TestCountWhitespaceStats:\n    def test_empty_string(self):\n        r = count_whitespace_stats(\"\")\n        assert r == {\"line_returns_count\": 0, \"unnecessary_space_count\": 0, \"total_chars\": 0}\n\n    def test_newlines_only(self):\n        r = count_whitespace_stats(\"\\n\\n\\n\")\n        assert r[\"line_returns_count\"] == 3\n        assert r[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 0\n        assert r[\"total_chars\"] == 3\n\n    def test_single_space_not_counted(self):\n        r = count_whitespace_stats(\"a b c\")\n        assert r[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 0\n\n    def test_double_space_counts_one(self):\n        r = count_whitespace_stats(\"a  b\")\n        assert r[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 1\n\n    def test_four_spaces_counts_three(self):\n        r = count_whitespace_stats(\"    \")\n        assert r[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 3\n\n    def test_two_runs(self):\n        # \"  \" gives 1, \"   \" gives 2 ‚Üí total 3\n        r = count_whitespace_stats(\"a  b   c\")\n        assert r[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 3\n\n    def test_total_chars(self):\n        r = count_whitespace_stats(\"hello\")\n        assert r[\"total_chars\"] == 5\n\n    def test_mixed_content(self):\n        r = count_whitespace_stats(\"line1\\nline2  extra\\n\")\n        assert r[\"line_returns_count\"] == 2\n        assert r[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 1\n        assert r[\"total_chars\"] == 19\n\n\nclass TestGetCanonicalModel:\n    def test_exact_match(self):\n        assert get_canonical_model(\"claude-sonnet-4-6\") == \"claude-sonnet-4-6\"\n\n    def test_date_suffix(self):\n        result = get_canonical_model(\"claude-opus-4-5-20241022\")\n        assert result == \"claude-opus-4-5\"\n\n    def test_longer_prefix_wins(self):\n        # \"claude-opus-4-5\" should match before \"claude-opus-4\"\n        assert get_canonical_model(\"claude-opus-4-5-extra\") == \"claude-opus-4-5\"\n\n    def test_unknown_model(self):\n        assert get_canonical_model(\"gpt-4-turbo\") is None\n\n    def test_empty_string(self):\n        assert get_canonical_model(\"\") is None\n\n    def test_all_known_models(self):\n        for model in MODEL_PRICING:\n            assert get_canonical_model(model) == model\n\n    def test_claude_haiku_variant(self):\n        assert get_canonical_model(\"claude-haiku-4-5-20250101\") == \"claude-haiku-4-5\"\n\n\nclass TestGetPricing:\n    def test_known_model_exact(self):\n        p = get_pricing(\"claude-sonnet-4-6\")\n        assert p is not None\n        assert \"input\" in p and \"output\" in p\n\n    def test_known_model_with_suffix(self):\n        p = get_pricing(\"claude-opus-4-5-20241022\")\n        assert p == MODEL_PRICING[\"claude-opus-4-5\"]\n\n    def test_unknown_model(self):\n        assert get_pricing(\"unknown-model\") is None\n\n\nclass TestSanitizePath:\n    def test_removes_query_string(self):\n        result = sanitize_path(\"/v1/messages?foo=bar\")\n        assert \"?\" not in result\n        assert \"foo\" not in result\n\n    def test_slashes_replaced(self):\n        result = sanitize_path(\"/v1/messages\")\n        assert \"/\" not in result\n\n    def test_strips_leading_trailing_underscores(self):\n        result = sanitize_path(\"/v1/messages\")\n        assert not result.startswith(\"_\")\n        assert not result.endswith(\"_\")\n\n    def test_special_chars_removed(self):\n        result = sanitize_path(\"/v1/mess@ages!\")\n        assert \"@\" not in result\n        assert \"!\" not in result\n\n    def test_truncated_at_80(self):\n        long_path = \"/v1/\" + \"a\" * 100\n        result = sanitize_path(long_path)\n        assert len(result) <= 80\n\n    def test_simple_path(self):\n        result = sanitize_path(\"/v1/messages\")\n        assert result == \"v1_messages\"\n\n    def test_alphanumeric_and_hyphens_preserved(self):\n        result = sanitize_path(\"/v1/my-endpoint_2\")\n        assert \"my-endpoint_2\" in result\n\n\nclass TestResolveReadFileName:\n    def test_read_file_compress(self):\n        assert _resolve_read_file_name(\"read_file\", {\"mode\": \"compress\"}) == \"read_file_compressed\"\n\n    def test_read_file_original(self):\n        assert _resolve_read_file_name(\"read_file\", {\"mode\": \"original\"}) == \"read_file_uncompressed\"\n\n    def test_read_file_empty_dict(self):\n        assert _resolve_read_file_name(\"read_file\", {}) == \"read_file_uncompressed\"\n\n    def test_read_file_non_dict(self):\n        assert _resolve_read_file_name(\"read_file\", \"not_a_dict\") == \"read_file_uncompressed\"\n\n    def test_other_tool_name_unchanged(self):\n        assert _resolve_read_file_name(\"Write\", {\"content\": \"x\"}) == \"Write\"\n        assert _resolve_read_file_name(\"Read\", {}) == \"Read\"\n        assert _resolve_read_file_name(\"edit_file\", {}) == \"edit_file\"\n\n\nclass TestFormatToolParams:\n    def test_empty_dict(self):\n        assert _format_tool_params({}) == \"\"\n\n    def test_string_value_quoted(self):\n        result = _format_tool_params({\"key\": \"value\"})\n        assert result == 'key=\"value\"'\n\n    def test_int_value_json(self):\n        result = _format_tool_params({\"count\": 5})\n        assert result == \"count=5\"\n\n    def test_bool_value_json(self):\n        result = _format_tool_params({\"flag\": True})\n        assert result == \"flag=true\"\n\n    def test_mixed_types(self):\n        result = _format_tool_params({\"path\": \"/foo\", \"lines\": 10})\n        assert 'path=\"/foo\"' in result\n        assert \"lines=10\" in result\n\n    def test_list_value_json(self):\n        result = _format_tool_params({\"items\": [1, 2]})\n        assert result == \"items=[1, 2]\"\n\n\nclass TestAgentColor:\n    def test_unknown_agent_is_hex(self):\n        color = _agent_color(\"mystery-agent\")\n        assert color.startswith(\"#\")\n        assert len(color) == 7\n\n    def test_deterministic(self):\n        assert _agent_color(\"foo\") == _agent_color(\"foo\")\n\n    def test_different_agents_different_colors(self):\n        assert _agent_color(\"agent-a\") != _agent_color(\"agent-b\")\n\n    def test_known_agent_colors_via_constant(self):\n        assert AGENT_COLORS[\"vix\"] == \"#7B2FBE\"\n        assert AGENT_COLORS[\"cc\"] == \"#D77656\"\n\n\nclass TestSystemPromptHash:\n    def _make_body(self, texts):\n        return {\"system\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": t} for t in texts]}\n\n    def test_cc_uses_index_2(self):\n        body = self._make_body([\"a\", \"b\", \"cc_prompt\"])\n        h = _system_prompt_hash(body, \"cc\")\n        assert h is not None\n        assert len(h) == 12\n\n    def test_vix_uses_index_0(self):\n        body = self._make_body([\"vix_prompt\", \"b\"])\n        h = _system_prompt_hash(body, \"vix\")\n        assert h is not None\n        assert len(h) == 12\n\n    def test_no_system_key(self):\n        assert _system_prompt_hash({}, \"cc\") is None\n\n    def test_index_out_of_range(self):\n        body = self._make_body([\"only_one\"])\n        assert _system_prompt_hash(body, \"cc\") is None  # index 2 doesn't exist\n\n    def test_empty_text_at_index(self):\n        body = {\"system\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"\"}, {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"\"}, {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"\"}]}\n        assert _system_prompt_hash(body, \"cc\") is None\n\n    def test_different_texts_different_hashes(self):\n        body1 = self._make_body([\"a\", \"b\", \"prompt_v1\"])\n        body2 = self._make_body([\"a\", \"b\", \"prompt_v2\"])\n        assert _system_prompt_hash(body1, \"cc\") != _system_prompt_hash(body2, \"cc\")\n\n    def test_unknown_agent_defaults_to_index_0(self):\n        body = self._make_body([\"idx0_text\"])\n        h = _system_prompt_hash(body, \"unknown_agent\")\n        assert h is not None\n\n    def test_empty_system_list(self):\n        assert _system_prompt_hash({\"system\": []}, \"vix\") is None\n\n\nclass TestGetFilePath:\n    def test_absolute_file_path_key(self):\n        assert _get_file_path({\"file_path\": \"/abs/path.py\"}) == \"/abs/path.py\"\n\n    def test_absolute_path_key(self):\n        assert _get_file_path({\"path\": \"/abs/path.py\"}) == \"/abs/path.py\"\n\n    def test_relative_path_joined_with_root(self):\n        result = _get_file_path({\"file_path\": \"src/foo.py\"})\n        assert result.endswith(\"src/foo.py\")\n        assert os.path.isabs(result)\n\n    def test_non_dict_returns_none(self):\n        assert _get_file_path(\"string\") is None\n        assert _get_file_path(None) is None\n        assert _get_file_path(42) is None\n\n    def test_neither_key_returns_none(self):\n        assert _get_file_path({\"other\": \"value\"}) is None\n\n    def test_file_path_takes_precedence_over_path(self):\n        result = _get_file_path({\"file_path\": \"/a/b.py\", \"path\": \"/c/d.py\"})\n        assert result == \"/a/b.py\"\n\n\nclass TestAggregateBySource:\n    def _empty_agg(self):\n        return {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n\n    def test_tool_results_accumulated(self):\n        agg = self._empty_agg()\n        by_source = {\n            \"input\": {\"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"tokens\": 10, \"dollars\": 0.001, \"chars\": 100}}},\n            \"output\": {},\n        }\n        _aggregate_by_source(agg, by_source)\n        assert agg[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"][\"tokens\"] == 10\n        assert agg[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"][\"chars\"] == 100\n\n        # Aggregate a second time\n        _aggregate_by_source(agg, by_source)\n        assert agg[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"][\"tokens\"] == 20\n\n    def test_tool_calls_accumulated(self):\n        agg = self._empty_agg()\n        by_source = {\n            \"input\": {\"tool_calls\": {\"Write\": {\"tokens\": 5, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 50}}},\n            \"output\": {},\n        }\n        _aggregate_by_source(agg, by_source)\n        assert agg[\"input\"][\"tool_calls\"][\"Write\"][\"tokens\"] == 5\n\n    def test_llm_text_accumulated(self):\n        agg = self._empty_agg()\n        by_source = {\n            \"input\": {},\n            \"output\": {\"llm_text\": {\"tokens\": 20, \"dollars\": 0.0003, \"chars\": 200}},\n        }\n        _aggregate_by_source(agg, by_source)\n        assert agg[\"output\"][\"llm_text\"][\"tokens\"] == 20\n\n        _aggregate_by_source(agg, by_source)\n        assert agg[\"output\"][\"llm_text\"][\"tokens\"] == 40\n\n    def test_output_tool_calls_accumulated(self):\n        agg = self._empty_agg()\n        by_source = {\n            \"input\": {},\n            \"output\": {\"tool_calls\": {\"__total\": {\"tokens\": 3, \"dollars\": 0.0, \"chars\": 30}}},\n        }\n        _aggregate_by_source(agg, by_source)\n        assert agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][\"__total\"][\"tokens\"] == 3\n\n    def test_empty_sections_skipped(self):\n        agg = self._empty_agg()\n        _aggregate_by_source(agg, {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}})\n        assert agg == {\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}}\n\n    def test_non_dict_entry_skipped(self):\n        agg = self._empty_agg()\n        by_source = {\n            \"input\": {\"tool_results\": {\"bad_entry\": \"not_a_dict\"}},\n            \"output\": {},\n        }\n        _aggregate_by_source(agg, by_source)\n        assert \"bad_entry\" not in agg[\"input\"].get(\"tool_results\", {})\n\n\nclass TestRoundBySource:\n    def test_rounds_input_tool_results(self):\n        agg = {\n            \"input\": {\"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"dollars\": 0.1234567, \"tokens\": 10, \"chars\": 5}}},\n            \"output\": {},\n        }\n        _round_by_source(agg)\n        assert agg[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"][\"dollars\"] == round(0.1234567, 6)\n\n    def test_rounds_input_tool_calls(self):\n        agg = {\n            \"input\": {\"tool_calls\": {\"Write\": {\"dollars\": 0.9999999}}},\n            \"output\": {},\n        }\n        _round_by_source(agg)\n        assert agg[\"input\"][\"tool_calls\"][\"Write\"][\"dollars\"] == round(0.9999999, 6)\n\n    def test_rounds_output_llm_text(self):\n        agg = {\n            \"input\": {},\n            \"output\": {\"llm_text\": {\"dollars\": 0.1111111, \"tokens\": 1, \"chars\": 1}},\n        }\n        _round_by_source(agg)\n        assert agg[\"output\"][\"llm_text\"][\"dollars\"] == round(0.1111111, 6)\n\n    def test_rounds_output_tool_calls(self):\n        agg = {\n            \"input\": {},\n            \"output\": {\"tool_calls\": {\"Read\": {\"dollars\": 0.2222222}}},\n        }\n        _round_by_source(agg)\n        assert agg[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"][\"Read\"][\"dollars\"] == round(0.2222222, 6)\n\n    def test_empty_sections_no_error(self):\n        _round_by_source({\"input\": {}, \"output\": {}})\n\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# 2. File I/O functions\n# ===========================================================================\n\n\nclass TestParseRequestBody:\n    def test_valid_json(self, tmp_path):\n        p = tmp_path / \"request.json\"\n        data = {\"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4-6\", \"messages\": []}\n        p.write_text(json.dumps(data))\n        result = parse_request_body(str(p))\n        assert result == data\n\n    def test_invalid_json(self, tmp_path):\n        p = tmp_path / \"request.json\"\n        p.write_text(\"not-valid-json{{{\")\n        assert parse_request_body(str(p)) is None\n\n    def test_empty_file_is_invalid_json(self, tmp_path):\n        p = tmp_path / \"request.json\"\n        p.write_text(\"\")\n        assert parse_request_body(str(p)) is None\n\n\nclass TestFormatHeaders:\n    def test_regular_header(self):\n        headers = make_headers_mock([(b\"content-type\", b\"application/json\")])\n        result = format_headers(headers)\n        assert \"content-type: application/json\" in result\n\n    def test_redacts_x_api_key(self):\n        headers = make_headers_mock([(b\"x-api-key\", b\"sk-secret123\")])\n        result = format_headers(headers)\n        assert \"REDACTED\" in result\n        assert \"sk-secret123\" not in result\n\n    def test_redacts_authorization(self):\n        headers = make_headers_mock([(b\"authorization\", b\"Bearer tok\")])\n        result = format_headers(headers)\n        assert \"REDACTED\" in result\n\n    def test_multiple_headers(self):\n        headers = make_headers_mock([\n            (b\"content-type\", b\"application/json\"),\n            (b\"x-api-key\", b\"secret\"),\n            (b\"accept\", b\"*/*\"),\n        ])\n        result = format_headers(headers)\n        lines = result.split(\"\\n\")\n        assert len(lines) == 3\n        assert \"REDACTED\" in lines[1]\n        assert \"application/json\" in lines[0]\n\n    def test_empty_headers(self):\n        headers = make_headers_mock([])\n        assert format_headers(headers) == \"\"\n\n\nclass TestExtractStopReason:\n    def test_sse_end_turn(self):\n        raw = 'data: {\"type\":\"message_delta\",\"delta\":{\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\"},\"usage\":{}}\\n'\n        assert extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"end_turn\"\n\n    def test_sse_tool_use(self):\n        raw = 'data: {\"type\": \"message_delta\",\"delta\":{\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\"},\"usage\":{}}\\n'\n        assert extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"tool_use\"\n\n    def test_nonstreaming_json_fallback(self):\n        raw = '{\"type\":\"message\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"content\":[]}\\n'\n        assert extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"end_turn\"\n\n    def test_unknown_when_no_match(self):\n        assert extract_stop_reason(\"no relevant content here\\n\") == \"unknown\"\n\n    def test_malformed_sse_skipped(self):\n        raw = \"data: {not valid json}\\ndata: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"message_delta\\\",\\\"delta\\\":{\\\"stop_reason\\\":\\\"max_tokens\\\"},\\\"usage\\\":{}}\\n\"\n        assert extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"max_tokens\"\n\n    def test_non_message_delta_type_skipped(self):\n        raw = 'data: {\"type\":\"message_start\",\"delta\":{\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\"}}\\n'\n        assert extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"unknown\"\n\n    def test_message_delta_without_stop_reason(self):\n        raw = 'data: {\"type\":\"message_delta\",\"delta\":{},\"usage\":{\"output_tokens\":5}}\\n'\n        assert extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"unknown\"\n\n    def test_non_message_type_json_fallback_skipped(self):\n        raw = '{\"type\":\"error\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\"}\\n'\n        assert extract_stop_reason(raw) == \"unknown\"\n\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# 3. File I/O functions using tmp_path\n# ===========================================================================\n\n\nclass TestWriteRequest:\n    def test_creates_request_headers_txt(self, tmp_path):\n        flow = make_mock_flow(\n            method=\"POST\",\n            url=\"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages\",\n            body='{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-6\"}',\n            req_headers=[(b\"content-type\", b\"application/json\")],\n        )\n        write_request(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        headers_file = tmp_path / \"request_headers.txt\"\n        assert headers_file.exists()\n        content = headers_file.read_text()\n        assert \"POST https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages\" in content\n        assert \"content-type: application/json\" in content\n\n    def test_creates_request_json_pretty_printed(self, tmp_path):\n        flow = make_mock_flow(body='{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-6\"}')\n        write_request(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        req_json = tmp_path / \"request.json\"\n        assert req_json.exists()\n        parsed = json.loads(req_json.read_text())\n        assert parsed[\"model\"] == \"claude-sonnet-4-6\"\n\n    def test_raw_fallback_for_invalid_json(self, tmp_path):\n        flow = make_mock_flow(body=\"not-json-body\")\n        write_request(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        req_json = tmp_path / \"request.json\"\n        assert req_json.exists()\n        assert req_json.read_text().strip() == \"not-json-body\"\n\n    def test_no_request_json_when_no_body(self, tmp_path):\n        flow = make_mock_flow(body=\"\")\n        write_request(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        assert not (tmp_path / \"request.json\").exists()\n\n    def test_redacts_api_key_in_headers(self, tmp_path):\n        flow = make_mock_flow(req_headers=[(b\"x-api-key\", b\"secret\")])\n        write_request(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        content = (tmp_path / \"request_headers.txt\").read_text()\n        assert \"REDACTED\" in content\n        assert \"secret\" not in content\n\n\nclass TestWriteResponse:\n    def test_no_file_when_response_is_none(self, tmp_path):\n        flow = make_mock_flow(no_response=True)\n        write_response(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        assert not (tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\").exists()\n\n    def test_creates_response_raw_txt(self, tmp_path):\n        flow = make_mock_flow(\n            status=200, reason=\"OK\",\n            resp_headers=[(b\"content-type\", b\"text/event-stream\")],\n            response_body=\"some response body\",\n        )\n        write_response(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        resp_file = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        assert resp_file.exists()\n        content = resp_file.read_text()\n        assert \"200 OK\" in content\n        assert \"content-type: text/event-stream\" in content\n        assert \"some response body\" in content\n\n    def test_response_without_body(self, tmp_path):\n        flow = make_mock_flow(status=204, reason=\"No Content\", response_body=\"\")\n        write_response(flow, str(tmp_path))\n        content = (tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\").read_text()\n        assert \"204 No Content\" in content\n\n\nclass TestExtractUsage:\n    def _make_response_dir(self, tmp_path, response_content):\n        d = tmp_path / \"agent\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n        d.mkdir(parents=True)\n        (d / \"response_raw.txt\").write_text(response_content)\n        return d\n\n    def test_sse_extracts_usage(self, tmp_path):\n        d = self._make_response_dir(tmp_path, SSE_RESPONSE_WITH_USAGE)\n        extract_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        usage_path = d / \"usage.json\"\n        assert usage_path.exists()\n        usage = json.loads(usage_path.read_text())\n        assert usage[\"input_tokens\"] == 10\n        assert usage[\"output_tokens\"] == 5\n        assert usage[\"cache_creation_input_tokens\"] == 2\n        assert usage[\"cache_read_input_tokens\"] == 3\n\n    def test_nonstreaming_fallback(self, tmp_path):\n        d = self._make_response_dir(tmp_path, NONSTREAM_RESPONSE)\n        extract_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert usage[\"input_tokens\"] == 8\n        assert usage[\"output_tokens\"] == 3\n\n    def test_timing_merged_and_file_removed(self, tmp_path):\n        d = self._make_response_dir(tmp_path, SSE_RESPONSE_WITH_USAGE)\n        timing = {\"request_start\": 1000.0, \"response_end\": 2000.0}\n        (d / \"timing.json\").write_text(json.dumps(timing))\n        extract_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        assert not (d / \"timing.json\").exists()\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert usage[\"timing\"][\"duration_ms\"] == 1000000\n\n    def test_timing_without_both_timestamps(self, tmp_path):\n        d = self._make_response_dir(tmp_path, SSE_RESPONSE_WITH_USAGE)\n        timing = {\"request_start\": 1000.0}\n        (d / \"timing.json\").write_text(json.dumps(timing))\n        extract_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert \"duration_ms\" not in usage.get(\"timing\", {})\n\n    def test_no_usage_in_response(self, tmp_path, capsys):\n        d = self._make_response_dir(tmp_path, \"200 OK\\n\\nno data here\\n\")\n        extract_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        assert not (d / \"usage.json\").exists()\n        captured = capsys.readouterr()\n        assert \"Warning\" in captured.out\n\n    def test_only_token_fields_kept(self, tmp_path):\n        d = self._make_response_dir(tmp_path, SSE_RESPONSE_WITH_USAGE)\n        extract_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        for key in usage:\n            if key not in (\"input_tokens\", \"output_tokens\", \"cache_creation_input_tokens\",\n                           \"cache_read_input_tokens\", \"timing\"):\n                assert False, f\"Unexpected key: {key}\"\n\n\nclass TestExtractPrompts:\n    def _make_request_dir(self, tmp_path, body):\n        d = tmp_path / \"agent\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n        d.mkdir(parents=True)\n        (d / \"request.json\").write_text(json.dumps(body))\n        return d\n\n    def test_extracts_system_prompt(self, tmp_path):\n        body = {\n            \"system\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"You are helpful.\"}],\n            \"messages\": [],\n        }\n        d = self._make_request_dir(tmp_path, body)\n        extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n        assert (d / \"system_prompt.md\").read_text() == \"You are helpful.\"\n\n    def test_concatenates_multiple_text_blocks(self, tmp_path):\n        body = {\n            \"system\": [\n                {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Part 1\"},\n                {\"type\": \"image\", \"source\": {}},\n                {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Part 2\"},\n            ],\n            \"messages\": [],\n        }\n        d = self._make_request_dir(tmp_path, body)\n        extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n        content = (d / \"system_prompt.md\").read_text()\n        assert \"Part 1\" in content\n        assert \"Part 2\" in content\n        assert \"image\" not in content.lower()\n\n    def test_no_system_prompt_file_when_empty(self, tmp_path):\n        body = {\"system\": [], \"messages\": []}\n        d = self._make_request_dir(tmp_path, body)\n        extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n        assert not (d / \"system_prompt.md\").exists()\n\n    def test_extracts_first_user_message(self, tmp_path):\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Hello there!\"}]},\n                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Hi!\"}]},\n            ],\n        }\n        d = self._make_request_dir(tmp_path, body)\n        extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n        assert (d / \"first_user_message.md\").read_text() == \"Hello there!\"\n\n    def test_skips_assistant_messages(self, tmp_path):\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"No\"}]},\n            ],\n        }\n        d = self._make_request_dir(tmp_path, body)\n        extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n        assert not (d / \"first_user_message.md\").exists()\n\n    def test_invalid_json_skipped(self, tmp_path, capsys):\n        d = tmp_path / \"agent\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n        d.mkdir(parents=True)\n        (d / \"request.json\").write_text(\"invalid json{{\")\n        extract_prompts(str(tmp_path))\n        captured = capsys.readouterr()\n        assert \"Warning\" in captured.out\n\n\nclass TestExtractReadFileWhitespace:\n    def test_read_file_string_content(self):\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"tu1\", \"name\": \"read_file\", \"input\": {\"mode\": \"original\"}}],\n                },\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"tu1\", \"content\": \"Hello  world\\n\"}],\n                },\n            ]\n        }\n        result = extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n        assert result[\"total_chars\"] == len(\"Hello  world\\n\")\n        assert result[\"line_returns_count\"] == 1\n        assert result[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 1\n\n    def test_read_file_list_content(self):\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"tu2\", \"name\": \"Read\", \"input\": {}}],\n                },\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"tu2\",\n                                 \"content\": [{\"text\": \"part1\"}, {\"text\": \"  part2\"}]}],\n                },\n            ]\n        }\n        result = extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n        assert result[\"total_chars\"] == len(\"part1  part2\")\n        assert result[\"unnecessary_space_count\"] == 1\n\n    def test_non_read_tool_excluded(self):\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"tu3\", \"name\": \"Write\", \"input\": {}}],\n                },\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"tu3\", \"content\": \"big text here\"}],\n                },\n            ]\n        }\n        result = extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n        assert result[\"total_chars\"] == 0\n\n    def test_compressed_read_file_included(self):\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"tu4\", \"name\": \"read_file\", \"input\": {\"mode\": \"compress\"}}],\n                },\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"tu4\", \"content\": \"compressed\\n\"}],\n                },\n            ]\n        }\n        result = extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n        assert result[\"total_chars\"] > 0\n\n    def test_unknown_tool_id_excluded(self):\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"unknown_id\", \"content\": \"should be excluded\"}],\n                },\n            ]\n        }\n        result = extract_read_file_whitespace(body)\n        assert result[\"total_chars\"] == 0\n\n\nclass TestCategorizeInputSources:\n    def _make_body_with_tool_result(self, n_user_msgs=2):\n        \"\"\"2 assistant+user pairs, tool result in each user msg.\"\"\"\n        messages = []\n        for i in range(n_user_msgs):\n            messages.append({\n                \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": f\"tu{i}\", \"name\": \"Read\", \"input\": {}}],\n            })\n            messages.append({\n                \"role\": \"user\",\n                \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": f\"tu{i}\", \"content\": f\"result {i}\"}],\n            })\n        return {\"messages\": messages}\n\n    def test_total_chars_is_json_length(self):\n        body = {\"messages\": [], \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4-6\"}\n        result = categorize_input_sources(body)\n        assert result[\"total_chars\"] == len(json.dumps(body))\n\n    def test_last_user_msg_is_cache_write(self):\n        body = self._make_body_with_tool_result(2)\n        result = categorize_input_sources(body)\n        tool_results = result[\"tool_results\"]\n        # Last user message ‚Üí cache_write\n        assert tool_results[\"Read\"][\"cache_write_chars\"] > 0\n\n    def test_earlier_user_msg_is_cache_read(self):\n        body = self._make_body_with_tool_result(2)\n        result = categorize_input_sources(body)\n        tool_results = result[\"tool_results\"]\n        assert tool_results[\"Read\"][\"cache_read_chars\"] > 0\n\n    def test_second_to_last_assistant_tool_use_is_cache_write(self):\n        body = self._make_body_with_tool_result(2)\n        result = categorize_input_sources(body)\n        # second-to-last message (index -2) is assistant before last user\n        tool_calls = result[\"tool_calls\"]\n        assert tool_calls[\"Read\"][\"cache_write_chars\"] > 0\n\n    def test_empty_messages(self):\n        result = categorize_input_sources({\"messages\": []})\n        assert result[\"tool_results\"] == {}\n        assert result[\"tool_calls\"] == {}\n\n    def test_read_file_resolved(self):\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"tu1\", \"name\": \"read_file\",\n                                 \"input\": {\"mode\": \"compress\"}}],\n                },\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"tu1\", \"content\": \"compressed data\"}],\n                },\n            ]\n        }\n        result = categorize_input_sources(body)\n        assert \"read_file_compressed\" in result[\"tool_results\"]\n\n\nclass TestCategorizeOutputSources:\n    def test_sse_text_block(self, tmp_path):\n        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        resp.write_text(SSE_RESPONSE_WITH_USAGE)\n        result = categorize_output_sources(str(resp))\n        assert result[\"llm_text\"] == len(\"Hello world\")\n        assert result[\"tool_calls\"] == {}\n\n    def test_sse_tool_use_block(self, tmp_path):\n        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        tool_json = json.dumps({\"file_path\": \"/foo.py\"})\n        content = (\n            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_start\",\"index\":0,\"content_block\":{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Write\"}}\\n'\n            f'data: {{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":{json.dumps(tool_json)}}}}}\\n'\n            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":0}\\n'\n        )\n        resp.write_text(content)\n        result = categorize_output_sources(str(resp))\n        assert \"Write\" in result[\"tool_calls\"]\n\n    def test_nonstreaming_fallback_text(self, tmp_path):\n        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        resp.write_text(NONSTREAM_RESPONSE)\n        result = categorize_output_sources(str(resp))\n        assert result[\"llm_text\"] == len(\"Hi\")\n\n    def test_nonstreaming_fallback_tool_use(self, tmp_path):\n        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        msg = {\n            \"type\": \"message\",\n            \"content\": [\n                {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": \"Read\", \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/a.py\"}, \"id\": \"tu1\"},\n            ],\n            \"stop_reason\": \"tool_use\",\n        }\n        resp.write_text(f\"200 OK\\n\\n{json.dumps(msg)}\")\n        result = categorize_output_sources(str(resp))\n        assert \"Read\" in result[\"tool_calls\"]\n\n    def test_empty_response(self, tmp_path):\n        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        resp.write_text(\"\")\n        result = categorize_output_sources(str(resp))\n        assert result[\"llm_text\"] == 0\n        assert result[\"tool_calls\"] == {}\n\n    def test_invalid_json_delta_gives_empty_input(self, tmp_path):\n        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        content = (\n            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_start\",\"index\":0,\"content_block\":{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Write\"}}\\n'\n            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"{invalid\"}}\\n'\n            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":0}\\n'\n        )\n        resp.write_text(content)\n        result = categorize_output_sources(str(resp))\n        # Should not raise, tool call should still be recorded\n        assert \"Write\" in result[\"tool_calls\"]\n\n    def test_read_file_name_resolved_in_sse(self, tmp_path):\n        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        tool_json = json.dumps({\"mode\": \"compress\"})\n        content = (\n            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_start\",\"index\":0,\"content_block\":{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"read_file\"}}\\n'\n            f'data: {{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":{json.dumps(tool_json)}}}}}\\n'\n            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":0}\\n'\n        )\n        resp.write_text(content)\n        result = categorize_output_sources(str(resp))\n        assert \"read_file_compressed\" in result[\"tool_calls\"]\n\n\nclass TestParseResponseContent:\n    def test_sse_text_block(self, tmp_path):\n        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        resp.write_text(SSE_RESPONSE_WITH_USAGE)\n        blocks = parse_response_content(str(resp))\n        assert len(blocks) == 1\n        assert blocks[0][\"type\"] == \"text\"\n        assert blocks[0][\"text\"] == \"Hello world\"\n\n    def test_sse_tool_use_block(self, tmp_path):\n        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        inp = {\"file_path\": \"/foo.py\", \"content\": \"hello\"}\n        inp_json = json.dumps(inp)\n        content = (\n            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_start\",\"index\":0,\"content_block\":{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Write\"}}\\n'\n            f'data: {{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":{json.dumps(inp_json)}}}}}\\n'\n            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":0}\\n'\n        )\n        resp.write_text(content)\n        blocks = parse_response_content(str(resp))\n        assert len(blocks) == 1\n        assert blocks[0][\"type\"] == \"tool_use\"\n        assert blocks[0][\"name\"] == \"Write\"\n\n    def test_nonstreaming_mixed_content(self, tmp_path):\n        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        msg = {\n            \"type\": \"message\",\n            \"content\": [\n                {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"I'll read the file.\"},\n                {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": \"Read\", \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/x.py\"}, \"id\": \"tu1\"},\n            ],\n            \"stop_reason\": \"tool_use\",\n        }\n        resp.write_text(f\"200 OK\\n\\n{json.dumps(msg)}\")\n        blocks = parse_response_content(str(resp))\n        assert len(blocks) == 2\n        assert blocks[0][\"type\"] == \"text\"\n        assert blocks[1][\"type\"] == \"tool_use\"\n\n    def test_empty_response_returns_empty_list(self, tmp_path):\n        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        resp.write_text(\"\")\n        assert parse_response_content(str(resp)) == []\n\n    def test_invalid_json_delta_gives_empty_input(self, tmp_path):\n        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        content = (\n            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_start\",\"index\":0,\"content_block\":{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Edit\"}}\\n'\n            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"{bad\"}}\\n'\n            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":0}\\n'\n        )\n        resp.write_text(content)\n        blocks = parse_response_content(str(resp))\n        assert blocks[0][\"input\"] == {}\n\n\nclass TestExportParsedResponse:\n    def test_writes_text_block(self, tmp_path):\n        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        resp.write_text(SSE_RESPONSE_WITH_USAGE)\n        out = tmp_path / \"response_parsed.txt\"\n        result = export_parsed_response(str(resp), str(out))\n        assert result is True\n        assert \"Hello world\" in out.read_text()\n\n    def test_writes_tool_use_block(self, tmp_path):\n        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        inp = {\"file_path\": \"/foo.py\"}\n        inp_json = json.dumps(inp)\n        content = (\n            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_start\",\"index\":0,\"content_block\":{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"name\":\"Read\"}}\\n'\n            f'data: {{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":{json.dumps(inp_json)}}}}}\\n'\n            'data: {\"type\":\"content_block_stop\",\"index\":0}\\n'\n        )\n        resp.write_text(content)\n        out = tmp_path / \"response_parsed.txt\"\n        result = export_parsed_response(str(resp), str(out))\n        assert result is True\n        text = out.read_text()\n        assert \"[Read(\" in text\n        assert \"file_path\" in text\n\n    def test_returns_false_for_empty_blocks(self, tmp_path):\n        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        resp.write_text(\"\")\n        out = tmp_path / \"response_parsed.txt\"\n        result = export_parsed_response(str(resp), str(out))\n        assert result is False\n        assert not out.exists()\n\n\nclass TestAttributeTokens:\n    def _make_usage(self, input_t=100, cw_t=50, cr_t=30, output_t=20,\n                    out_dollars=0.0003):\n        return {\n            \"cost\": {\n                \"input\": {\"tokens\": input_t, \"dollars\": input_t * 3e-6},\n                \"cache_write\": {\"tokens\": cw_t, \"dollars\": cw_t * 3.75e-6},\n                \"cache_read\": {\"tokens\": cr_t, \"dollars\": cr_t * 0.30e-6},\n                \"output\": {\"tokens\": output_t, \"dollars\": round(out_dollars, 6)},\n            }\n        }\n\n    def _pricing(self):\n        return {\"input\": 3e-6, \"cache_write\": 3.75e-6, \"cache_read\": 0.30e-6, \"output\": 15e-6}\n\n    def test_output_distributed_proportionally(self):\n        usage = self._make_usage(output_t=100, out_dollars=0.0015)\n        input_sources = {\"total_chars\": 1000, \"tool_results\": {}, \"tool_calls\": {}}\n        output_sources = {\"llm_text\": 80, \"tool_calls\": {\"Write\": 20}}\n        result = attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, self._pricing())\n        llm = result[\"output\"][\"llm_text\"]\n        assert llm[\"tokens\"] == 80  # 80% of 100\n        assert llm[\"chars\"] == 80\n        tc = result[\"output\"][\"tool_calls\"]\n        assert \"__total\" in tc\n        assert tc[\"Write\"][\"tokens\"] == 20\n\n    def test_zero_total_chars_skips_input(self):\n        usage = self._make_usage()\n        input_sources = {\"total_chars\": 0, \"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 10, \"cache_read_chars\": 0}}, \"tool_calls\": {}}\n        output_sources = {\"llm_text\": 0, \"tool_calls\": {}}\n        result = attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, self._pricing())\n        assert result[\"input\"] == {}\n\n    def test_zero_output_chars_skips_output(self):\n        usage = self._make_usage()\n        input_sources = {\"total_chars\": 1000, \"tool_results\": {}, \"tool_calls\": {}}\n        output_sources = {\"llm_text\": 0, \"tool_calls\": {}}\n        result = attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, self._pricing())\n        assert result[\"output\"] == {}\n\n    def test_input_tool_results_attributed(self):\n        usage = self._make_usage(input_t=100, cw_t=0, cr_t=0)\n        input_sources = {\n            \"total_chars\": 1000,\n            \"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"cache_write_chars\": 200, \"cache_read_chars\": 100}},\n            \"tool_calls\": {},\n        }\n        output_sources = {\"llm_text\": 0, \"tool_calls\": {}}\n        result = attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, self._pricing())\n        assert \"tool_results\" in result[\"input\"]\n        read_entry = result[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"]\n        assert read_entry[\"chars\"] == 300\n\n    def test_empty_tool_results_not_in_output(self):\n        usage = self._make_usage()\n        input_sources = {\"total_chars\": 1000, \"tool_results\": {}, \"tool_calls\": {}}\n        output_sources = {\"llm_text\": 50, \"tool_calls\": {}}\n        result = attribute_tokens(input_sources, output_sources, usage, self._pricing())\n        assert \"tool_results\" not in result[\"input\"]\n\n\nclass TestExtractFileOps:\n    def _write_response(self, tmp_path, blocks):\n        \"\"\"Write a non-streaming JSON response with given content blocks.\"\"\"\n        msg = {\"type\": \"message\", \"content\": blocks, \"stop_reason\": \"tool_use\"}\n        resp = tmp_path / \"response_raw.txt\"\n        resp.write_text(f\"200 OK\\n\\n{json.dumps(msg)}\")\n        return str(resp)\n\n    def test_read_file_from_tool_result_string(self, tmp_path):\n        response_path = self._write_response(tmp_path, [])\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"tu1\", \"name\": \"read_file\",\n                                 \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/abs/file.py\", \"mode\": \"original\"}}],\n                },\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"tu1\",\n                                 \"content\": \"file content here\"}],\n                },\n            ]\n        }\n        result = extract_file_ops(body, response_path)\n        inp = result[\"input\"]\n        assert inp[\"unique_files_read\"] == 1\n        assert inp[\"total_read_chars\"] == len(\"file content here\")\n        assert \"/abs/file.py\" in inp[\"per_file\"]\n\n    def test_read_file_list_content(self, tmp_path):\n        response_path = self._write_response(tmp_path, [])\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"tu2\", \"name\": \"Read\",\n                                 \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/abs/b.py\"}}],\n                },\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"tu2\",\n                                 \"content\": [{\"text\": \"part1\"}, {\"text\": \"part2\"}]}],\n                },\n            ]\n        }\n        result = extract_file_ops(body, response_path)\n        assert result[\"input\"][\"total_read_chars\"] == len(\"part1\") + len(\"part2\")\n\n    def test_write_tool_counts_content(self, tmp_path):\n        write_block = {\n            \"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": \"Write\", \"id\": \"tw1\",\n            \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/abs/out.py\", \"content\": \"hello world\"},\n        }\n        response_path = self._write_response(tmp_path, [write_block])\n        result = extract_file_ops({}, response_path)\n        out = result[\"output\"]\n        assert out[\"unique_files_written\"] == 1\n        assert out[\"total_write_chars\"] == len(\"hello world\")\n        assert \"/abs/out.py\" in out[\"per_file\"]\n\n    def test_edit_tool_counts_new_string(self, tmp_path):\n        edit_block = {\n            \"type\": \"tool_use\", \"name\": \"Edit\", \"id\": \"te1\",\n            \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/abs/edit.py\", \"new_string\": \"replacement\"},\n        }\n        response_path = self._write_response(tmp_path, [edit_block])\n        result = extract_file_ops({}, response_path)\n        assert result[\"output\"][\"total_write_chars\"] == len(\"replacement\")\n\n    def test_file_size_none_on_oserror(self, tmp_path):\n        response_path = self._write_response(tmp_path, [])\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"tu3\", \"name\": \"Read\",\n                                 \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/nonexistent/file.py\"}}],\n                },\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [{\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"tu3\",\n                                 \"content\": \"data\"}],\n                },\n            ]\n        }\n        result = extract_file_ops(body, response_path)\n        fp = \"/nonexistent/file.py\"\n        assert result[\"input\"][\"per_file\"][fp][\"file_size\"] is None\n\n    def test_deduplication_via_tool_ids(self, tmp_path):\n        response_path = self._write_response(tmp_path, [])\n        body = {\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": [\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"tu4\", \"name\": \"Read\", \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/abs/dup.py\"}},\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_use\", \"id\": \"tu5\", \"name\": \"Read\", \"input\": {\"file_path\": \"/abs/dup.py\"}},\n                    ],\n                },\n                {\n                    \"role\": \"user\",\n                    \"content\": [\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"tu4\", \"content\": \"aaa\"},\n                        {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": \"tu5\", \"content\": \"bbb\"},\n                    ],\n                },\n            ]\n        }\n        result = extract_file_ops(body, response_path)\n        pf = result[\"input\"][\"per_file\"][\"/abs/dup.py\"]\n        assert pf[\"calls\"] == 2\n        assert pf[\"chars\"] == len(\"aaa\") + len(\"bbb\")\n\n\nclass TestCalculateCosts:\n    def _make_flow_dir(self, tmp_path, model, tokens):\n        d = tmp_path / \"agent\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n        d.mkdir(parents=True)\n        body = {\"model\": model, \"messages\": []}\n        (d / \"request.json\").write_text(json.dumps(body))\n        (d / \"usage.json\").write_text(json.dumps(tokens))\n        return d\n\n    def test_known_model_cost_computed(self, tmp_path):\n        tokens = {\n            \"input_tokens\": 100, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0,\n            \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 0, \"output_tokens\": 50,\n        }\n        d = self._make_flow_dir(tmp_path, \"claude-sonnet-4-6\", tokens)\n        calculate_costs(str(tmp_path))\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        cost = usage[\"cost\"]\n        assert cost[\"input\"][\"tokens\"] == 100\n        assert cost[\"output\"][\"tokens\"] == 50\n        assert cost[\"total\"][\"tokens\"] == 150\n        # Check dollars are positive\n        assert cost[\"input\"][\"dollars\"] > 0\n        assert cost[\"output\"][\"dollars\"] > 0\n\n    def test_top_level_token_keys_removed(self, tmp_path):\n        tokens = {\n            \"input_tokens\": 10, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0,\n            \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 0, \"output_tokens\": 5,\n        }\n        d = self._make_flow_dir(tmp_path, \"claude-sonnet-4-6\", tokens)\n        calculate_costs(str(tmp_path))\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert \"input_tokens\" not in usage\n        assert \"output_tokens\" not in usage\n\n    def test_canonical_model_added(self, tmp_path):\n        tokens = {\"input_tokens\": 10, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0,\n                  \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 0, \"output_tokens\": 5}\n        d = self._make_flow_dir(tmp_path, \"claude-opus-4-5-20241022\", tokens)\n        calculate_costs(str(tmp_path))\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert usage[\"model\"] == \"claude-opus-4-5\"\n\n    def test_unknown_model_skipped(self, tmp_path, capsys):\n        tokens = {\"input_tokens\": 10, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": 0,\n                  \"cache_read_input_tokens\": 0, \"output_tokens\": 5}\n        d = self._make_flow_dir(tmp_path, \"gpt-4-turbo\", tokens)\n        calculate_costs(str(tmp_path))\n        captured = capsys.readouterr()\n        assert \"Warning\" in captured.out\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert \"cost\" not in usage\n\n    def test_missing_model_field_skipped(self, tmp_path):\n        d = tmp_path / \"agent\" / \"1\" / \"1\"\n        d.mkdir(parents=True)\n        (d / \"request.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"messages\": []}))\n        (d / \"usage.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"input_tokens\": 10}))\n        calculate_costs(str(tmp_path))\n        usage = json.loads((d / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert \"cost\" not in usage\n\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# 4. mitmproxy-dependent functions\n# ===========================================================================\n\nclass TestRedactFlowFiles:\n    def test_no_flow_files_returns_immediately(self, tmp_path, capsys):\n        redact_flow_files(str(tmp_path))\n        out = capsys.readouterr().out\n        # Should print \"Redacted API keys in 0 flow files\" or just return\n        assert \"0\" in out or out == \"\"\n\n    def test_flow_file_with_api_key_redacted(self, tmp_path, capsys):\n        from mitmproxy.exceptions import FlowReadException\n\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"test.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"dummy\")\n\n        mock_flow = make_mock_flow()\n        mock_flow.request.headers.get = MagicMock(return_value=\"sk-secret\")\n\n        with patch(\"export_flows.glob.glob\", return_value=[str(flow_file)]), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.FlowReader\") as MockReader, \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.FlowWriter\") as MockWriter, \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.isinstance\", side_effect=lambda obj, cls: cls == __builtins__.__class__ or True if cls.__name__ == \"HTTPFlow\" else isinstance(obj, cls)) if False else patch(\"builtins.open\", mock_open()):\n            # Simpler approach: patch open and FlowReader directly\n            pass\n\n        # Use a more straightforward mock approach\n        mock_flow2 = MagicMock()\n        mock_flow2.request.headers.get = MagicMock(side_effect=lambda h: b\"sk-secret\" if h == b\"x-api-key\" else None)\n\n        reader_instance = MagicMock()\n        reader_instance.stream.return_value = iter([mock_flow2])\n\n        writer_instance = MagicMock()\n\n        with patch(\"export_flows.glob.glob\", return_value=[str(flow_file)]), \\\n             patch(\"builtins.open\", mock_open(read_data=b\"\")), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.FlowReader\", return_value=reader_instance), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.FlowWriter\", return_value=writer_instance), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.isinstance\") as mock_isinstance:\n            mock_isinstance.side_effect = lambda obj, cls: True  # treat all as HTTPFlow\n            redact_flow_files(str(tmp_path))\n\n    def test_flow_read_exception_skipped(self, tmp_path, capsys):\n        from mitmproxy.exceptions import FlowReadException\n\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"bad.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"corrupt data\")\n\n        reader_instance = MagicMock()\n        reader_instance.stream.side_effect = FlowReadException(\"corrupt\")\n\n        with patch(\"export_flows.glob.glob\", return_value=[str(flow_file)]), \\\n             patch(\"builtins.open\", mock_open(read_data=b\"\")), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.FlowReader\", return_value=reader_instance):\n            redact_flow_files(str(tmp_path))\n\n        captured = capsys.readouterr()\n        assert \"Skipping\" in captured.out or \"bad.flow\" in captured.out\n\n\nclass TestExportFlows:\n    def _make_flow_reader_mock(self, flows):\n        reader_instance = MagicMock()\n        reader_instance.__enter__ = MagicMock(return_value=reader_instance)\n        reader_instance.__exit__ = MagicMock(return_value=False)\n        reader_instance.stream.return_value = iter(flows)\n        return reader_instance\n\n    def test_no_flow_files_prints_message(self, tmp_path, capsys):\n        with patch(\"export_flows.glob.glob\", return_value=[]):\n            _export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(tmp_path / \"out\"))\n        assert \"No\" in capsys.readouterr().out\n\n    def test_skips_count_token_url(self, tmp_path, capsys):\n        out_dir = tmp_path / \"out\"\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"vix.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"\")\n\n        count_token_flow = make_mock_flow(url=\"https://api.example.com/count_token\")\n\n        reader_instance = self._make_flow_reader_mock([count_token_flow])\n\n        with patch(\"export_flows.glob.glob\", return_value=[str(flow_file)]), \\\n             patch(\"builtins.open\", mock_open(read_data=b\"\")), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.FlowReader\", return_value=reader_instance), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.os.makedirs\"), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.os.path.exists\", return_value=False), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.shutil.rmtree\"):\n            _export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(out_dir))\n\n        assert \"Exported 0 flows\" in capsys.readouterr().out\n\n    def test_skips_quota_requests(self, tmp_path, capsys):\n        out_dir = tmp_path / \"out\"\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"vix.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"\")\n\n        quota_body = json.dumps({\"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"quota\"}]})\n        quota_flow = make_mock_flow(body=quota_body)\n\n        reader_instance = self._make_flow_reader_mock([quota_flow])\n\n        with patch(\"export_flows.glob.glob\", return_value=[str(flow_file)]), \\\n             patch(\"builtins.open\", mock_open(read_data=b\"\")), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.FlowReader\", return_value=reader_instance), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.os.makedirs\"), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.os.path.exists\", return_value=False), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.shutil.rmtree\"):\n            _export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(out_dir))\n\n        assert \"Exported 0 flows\" in capsys.readouterr().out\n\n    def test_vix_step_increments_on_end_turn(self, tmp_path, capsys):\n        out_dir = tmp_path / \"out\"\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"vix.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"\")\n\n        end_turn_resp = (\n            'data: {\"type\":\"message_delta\",\"delta\":{\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\"},\"usage\":{\"output_tokens\":1}}\\n'\n        )\n        flow1 = make_mock_flow(response_body=end_turn_resp)\n        flow2 = make_mock_flow(response_body=\"no stop reason\")\n\n        reader_instance = self._make_flow_reader_mock([flow1, flow2])\n\n        created_dirs = []\n\n        def mock_makedirs(path, exist_ok=False):\n            created_dirs.append(path)\n\n        with patch(\"export_flows.glob.glob\", return_value=[str(flow_file)]), \\\n             patch(\"builtins.open\", mock_open(read_data=b\"\")), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.FlowReader\", return_value=reader_instance), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.os.makedirs\", side_effect=mock_makedirs), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.os.path.exists\", return_value=False), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.shutil.rmtree\"), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.write_request\"), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.write_response\"):\n            _export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(out_dir))\n\n        # Flow1 in step 1, flow2 in step 2 (after end_turn)\n        dirs_str = \" \".join(created_dirs)\n        assert \"vix\" in dirs_str.lower() or \"out\" in dirs_str.lower()\n\n    def test_cc_step_increments_on_prompt_hash_change(self, tmp_path, capsys):\n        out_dir = tmp_path / \"out\"\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"cc.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"\")\n\n        body1 = json.dumps({\n            \"system\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"a\"}, {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"b\"}, {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"prompt_v1\"}],\n            \"messages\": [],\n        })\n        body2 = json.dumps({\n            \"system\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"a\"}, {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"b\"}, {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"prompt_v2\"}],\n            \"messages\": [],\n        })\n\n        flow1 = make_mock_flow(body=body1)\n        flow2 = make_mock_flow(body=body2)\n\n        reader_instance = self._make_flow_reader_mock([flow1, flow2])\n        created_dirs = []\n\n        def mock_makedirs(path, exist_ok=False):\n            created_dirs.append(path)\n\n        with patch(\"export_flows.glob.glob\", return_value=[str(flow_file)]), \\\n             patch(\"builtins.open\", mock_open(read_data=b\"\")), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.FlowReader\", return_value=reader_instance), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.os.makedirs\", side_effect=mock_makedirs), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.os.path.exists\", return_value=False), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.shutil.rmtree\"), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.write_request\"), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.write_response\"):\n            _export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(out_dir))\n\n        # Step 2 directory should be created for the second flow\n        step2_dirs = [d for d in created_dirs if \"/2/\" in d or \"\\\\2\\\\\" in d]\n        assert len(step2_dirs) > 0\n\n    def test_flow_read_exception_skipped(self, tmp_path, capsys):\n        from mitmproxy.exceptions import FlowReadException\n        out_dir = tmp_path / \"out\"\n        flow_file = tmp_path / \"vix.flow\"\n        flow_file.write_bytes(b\"\")\n\n        reader_instance = self._make_flow_reader_mock([])\n        reader_instance.stream.side_effect = FlowReadException(\"bad\")\n\n        with patch(\"export_flows.glob.glob\", return_value=[str(flow_file)]), \\\n             patch(\"builtins.open\", mock_open(read_data=b\"\")), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.FlowReader\", return_value=reader_instance), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.os.makedirs\"), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.os.path.exists\", return_value=False), \\\n             patch(\"export_flows.shutil.rmtree\"):\n            _export_flows(str(tmp_path), str(out_dir))\n\n        assert \"Skipping\" in capsys.readouterr().out\n\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# 5. summarize_usage\n# ===========================================================================\n\nclass TestSummarizeUsage:\n    def _make_agent_dir(self, base, agent_name, steps):\n        \"\"\"Create agent/step/request/usage.json structure.\n\n        steps: list of lists of usage dicts (outer = step, inner = requests in that step)\n        \"\"\"\n        agent_dir = base / agent_name\n        for step_idx, requests in enumerate(steps, 1):\n            for req_idx, usage in enumerate(requests, 1):\n                req_dir = agent_dir / str(step_idx) / str(req_idx)\n                req_dir.mkdir(parents=True)\n                (req_dir / \"usage.json\").write_text(json.dumps(usage))\n        return agent_dir\n\n    def _make_usage(self, model=\"claude-sonnet-4-6\", input_t=100, output_t=50,\n                    req_start=1000.0, resp_end=2000.0, duration_ms=1000000):\n        return {\n            \"model\": model,\n            \"cost\": {\n                \"input\": {\"tokens\": input_t, \"dollars\": input_t * 3e-6},\n                \"cache_write\": {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0},\n                \"cache_read\": {\"tokens\": 0, \"dollars\": 0.0},\n                \"output\": {\"tokens\": output_t, \"dollars\": output_t * 15e-6},\n                \"total\": {\"tokens\": input_t + output_t, \"dollars\": (input_t * 3e-6 + output_t * 15e-6)},\n            },\n            \"timing\": {\n                \"request_start\": req_start,\n                \"response_end\": resp_end,\n                \"duration_ms\": duration_ms,\n            },\n        }\n\n    def test_creates_usage_json_for_agent(self, tmp_path):\n        usage = self._make_usage()\n        self._make_agent_dir(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[usage]])\n        summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary_path = tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\"\n        assert summary_path.exists()\n\n    def test_summary_has_correct_structure(self, tmp_path):\n        usage = self._make_usage()\n        self._make_agent_dir(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[usage]])\n        summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert summary[\"title\"] == \"vix\"\n        assert \"by_model\" in summary\n        assert \"by_step\" in summary\n        assert \"total\" in summary\n        assert \"color\" in summary\n\n    def test_known_agent_color(self, tmp_path):\n        usage = self._make_usage()\n        self._make_agent_dir(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[usage]])\n        summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert summary[\"color\"] == AGENT_COLORS[\"vix\"]\n\n    def test_unknown_agent_gets_md5_color(self, tmp_path):\n        usage = self._make_usage()\n        self._make_agent_dir(tmp_path, \"mystery_agent\", [[usage]])\n        summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"mystery_agent\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert summary[\"color\"].startswith(\"#\")\n        assert len(summary[\"color\"]) == 7\n\n    def test_aggregates_multiple_requests(self, tmp_path):\n        u1 = self._make_usage(input_t=100, output_t=50)\n        u2 = self._make_usage(input_t=200, output_t=80)\n        self._make_agent_dir(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[u1, u2]])\n        summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        total = summary[\"total\"]\n        assert total[\"request_count\"] == 2\n        assert total[\"cost\"][\"input\"][\"tokens\"] == 300\n        assert total[\"cost\"][\"output\"][\"tokens\"] == 130\n\n    def test_by_step_aggregation(self, tmp_path):\n        u1 = self._make_usage(input_t=100)\n        u2 = self._make_usage(input_t=200)\n        self._make_agent_dir(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[u1], [u2]])\n        summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert \"1\" in summary[\"by_step\"]\n        assert \"2\" in summary[\"by_step\"]\n        assert summary[\"by_step\"][\"1\"][\"cost\"][\"input\"][\"tokens\"] == 100\n        assert summary[\"by_step\"][\"2\"][\"cost\"][\"input\"][\"tokens\"] == 200\n\n    def test_by_model_aggregation(self, tmp_path):\n        u1 = self._make_usage(model=\"claude-sonnet-4-6\", input_t=100)\n        u2 = self._make_usage(model=\"claude-opus-4-5\", input_t=200)\n        self._make_agent_dir(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[u1, u2]])\n        summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert \"claude-sonnet-4-6\" in summary[\"by_model\"]\n        assert \"claude-opus-4-5\" in summary[\"by_model\"]\n\n    def test_timing_wall_clock_computed(self, tmp_path):\n        u1 = self._make_usage(req_start=1000.0, resp_end=2000.0, duration_ms=1000000)\n        u2 = self._make_usage(req_start=1500.0, resp_end=3000.0, duration_ms=1500000)\n        self._make_agent_dir(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[u1, u2]])\n        summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        timing = summary[\"total\"][\"timing\"]\n        # wall_clock_ms = (max_resp_end - min_req_start) * 1000\n        assert timing[\"wall_clock_ms\"] == round((3000.0 - 1000.0) * 1000)\n\n    def test_avg_duration_ms_computed(self, tmp_path):\n        u1 = self._make_usage(duration_ms=1000)\n        u2 = self._make_usage(duration_ms=3000)\n        self._make_agent_dir(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[u1, u2]])\n        summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        assert summary[\"total\"][\"timing\"][\"avg_duration_ms\"] == 2000\n\n    def test_skips_dirs_without_numbered_subdirs(self, tmp_path):\n        # Create an agent dir but only with non-numeric subdirs\n        agent_dir = tmp_path / \"not_an_agent\"\n        agent_dir.mkdir()\n        (agent_dir / \"some_file.json\").write_text(\"{}\")\n\n        summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        assert not (agent_dir / \"usage.json\").exists()\n\n    def test_skips_non_directory_entries(self, tmp_path):\n        # Create a plain file in output_dir\n        (tmp_path / \"somefile.txt\").write_text(\"hello\")\n        usage = self._make_usage()\n        self._make_agent_dir(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[usage]])\n        # Should not raise\n        summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n\n    def test_file_ops_finalized(self, tmp_path):\n        usage = self._make_usage()\n        usage[\"file_ops\"] = {\n            \"input\": {\n                \"unique_files_read\": 1,\n                \"total_read_chars\": 100,\n                \"per_file\": {\"/a.py\": {\"calls\": 1, \"chars\": 100, \"tool_ids\": {\"tu1\": 100}, \"file_size\": 200}},\n            },\n            \"output\": {\n                \"files_written\": 1,\n                \"unique_files_written\": 1,\n                \"total_write_chars\": 50,\n                \"per_file\": {\"/b.py\": {\"calls\": 1, \"chars\": 50, \"tool_ids\": {\"tw1\": 50}, \"file_size\": 100}},\n            },\n        }\n        self._make_agent_dir(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[usage]])\n        summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        total_file_ops = summary[\"total\"][\"file_ops\"]\n        assert total_file_ops[\"input\"][\"unique_files_read\"] == 1\n        # tool_ids should be removed\n        for fp, stats in total_file_ops[\"input\"][\"per_file\"].items():\n            assert \"tool_ids\" not in stats\n\n    def test_by_source_aggregated(self, tmp_path):\n        usage = self._make_usage()\n        usage[\"by_source\"] = {\n            \"input\": {\"tool_results\": {\"Read\": {\"tokens\": 50, \"dollars\": 0.0001, \"chars\": 500}}},\n            \"output\": {\"llm_text\": {\"tokens\": 20, \"dollars\": 0.0003, \"chars\": 200}},\n        }\n        self._make_agent_dir(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[usage, usage]])\n        summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        by_source = summary[\"by_source\"]\n        assert by_source[\"input\"][\"tool_results\"][\"Read\"][\"tokens\"] == 100\n\n    def test_read_file_whitespace_aggregated(self, tmp_path):\n        usage = self._make_usage()\n        usage[\"read_file_whitespace\"] = {\n            \"line_returns_count\": 10,\n            \"unnecessary_space_count\": 5,\n            \"total_chars\": 200,\n        }\n        self._make_agent_dir(tmp_path, \"vix\", [[usage, usage]])\n        summarize_usage(str(tmp_path))\n        summary = json.loads((tmp_path / \"vix\" / \"usage.json\").read_text())\n        ws = summary[\"read_file_whitespace\"]\n        assert ws[\"line_returns_count\"] == 20\n        assert ws[\"total_chars\"] == 400\n"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013cUbN94nuTdnaEAbvTdNxs","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /workspace/evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let's run the tests to check coverage:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UUsoGYUXd9wSgeNGy9mWDf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python -m pytest evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py -v --tb=short 2>&1 | head -120","description":"Run tests to check initial pass rate","timeout":120000}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UUsoGYUXd9wSgeNGy9mWDf","type":"tool_result","content":"/bin/bash: line 1: python: command not found","is_error":false}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LXRC8hyLhdoLt3yyJV9sxo","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -m pytest evaluation/usage/test_export_flows.py -v --tb=short 2>&1 | head -150","description":"Run tests to check initial pass rate","timeout":120000}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LXRC8hyLhdoLt3yyJV9sxo","type":"tool_result","content":"/usr/bin/python3: No module named pytest","is_error":false}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LAZecCiKCkHWz2sV48Zh3d","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"pip3 install pytest pytest-cov 2>&1 | tail -5","description":"Install pytest and coverage","timeout":60000}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LAZecCiKCkHWz2sV48Zh3d","type":"tool_result","content":"    See /usr/share/doc/python3.11/README.venv for more information.\n\nnote: If you believe this is a mistake, please contact your Python insta